{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01ERdT2x7dFH1V5F3Lg1VCep","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# Implementation Plan: Multi-Format Diagram Support & Markdown Editing\n     2→\n     3→**Status:** PLANNING — Iteration 2 (refined, codebase-verified)\n     4→**Created:** 2026-02-15\n     5→**Updated:** 2026-02-15 (Iteration 2 — settings path fix, CDN verification, precise line refs)\n     6→**Spec Source:** `domain-requirements.md` Expansion section (added 2026-02-15)\n     7→**Parent Feature:** `.vista/features/diagram_representations/`\n     8→\n     9→---\n    10→\n    11→## Context\n    12→\n    13→The existing diagram_representations feature is largely delivered (Phases 1-4 complete, Phase 5 partial). The domain-requirements.md has been expanded with three new areas:\n    14→\n    15→1. **Multi-Format Rendering** — PlantUML (.puml), D2 (.d2), Graphviz (.dot), Markdown (.md)\n    16→2. **Markdown Inline Editing** — View/edit toggle, save to disk via PUT API, cancel/discard\n    17→3. **Manifest & Type System Updates** — Extended type enum, renderer dispatch, file extension mapping\n    18→\n    19→This plan covers implementing these expansion requirements on top of the existing codebase.\n    20→\n    21→---\n    22→\n    23→## Current State Assessment (Verified Iteration 2)\n    24→\n    25→### What Exists (Working)\n    26→\n    27→| Component | Status | Location (verified) |\n    28→|-----------|--------|---------------------|\n    29→| Mermaid rendering | Complete | `architecture.html:1288-1307` — `mermaid.render()` |\n    30→| Renderer dispatch | Partial — only `.mmd` check + fallback `<pre>` | `architecture.html:1288-1311` — `renderDiagramContent()` |\n    31→| `_arch.json` schema | `type` enum: `[\"mermaid\", \"drawio\"]` only | `arch-schema.json:29` |\n    32→| Diagram watcher | Watches `.mmd` and `.drawio` only | `diagram_watcher.py:26,124` — `WATCH_EXTENSIONS` (defined twice) |\n    33→| `_detect_diagram_type()` | Parses mermaid subtype from first line of `.mmd` | `diagram_watcher.py:102-118` |\n    34→| Manifest auto-update | Scans `.mmd`/`.drawio` in arch dir, builds `_arch.json` | `diagram_watcher.py:232-256` — `_update_manifest_sync()` |\n    35→| API: GET manifest | Complete | `architecture.py:15-26` |\n    36→| API: GET file | Complete (text/plain for .mmd, application/xml for .drawio) | `architecture.py:29-48` — `get_arch_file()` |\n    37→| API: PUT file | **Does not exist** | Needed for markdown save |\n    38→| Path traversal protection | Complete | `progress_service.py:78-97` — `read_arch_file()` |\n    39→| Pan/zoom per diagram | Complete | `architecture.html:1323-1375` |\n    40→| Settings file | Located at `~/.vista/settings.json`, managed by `config.py` | `config.py:23-35` — `_resolve_settings_file()` |\n    41→| `plantuml_server_url` | **Does not exist** anywhere | Not in `config.py` or any settings |\n    42→| CDN: mermaid.js | Loaded | `architecture.html:6` |\n    43→| CDN: marked.js | Loaded (for chat markdown) | `architecture.html:7` |\n    44→| Test suite | 29 tests in `test_architecture.py`, 24 in `test_diagram_watcher.py` | All passing (139 total) |\n    45→\n    46→### What Needs to Change\n    47→\n    48→1. **arch-schema.json** (line 29) — Extend `type` enum from 2 to 6 values\n    49→2. **diagram_watcher.py** (lines 26, 124) — Extend `WATCH_EXTENSIONS` and `_detect_diagram_type()` for new formats\n    50→3. **progress_service.py** — Add `write_arch_file()` method (after `read_arch_file()` at line 97)\n    51→4. **architecture.py** — Add `PUT` endpoint, update content-type mapping (lines 40-46)\n    52→5. **architecture.html** — Refactor renderer dispatch (lines 1288-1311), add 4 new renderers + markdown edit mode\n    53→6. **config.py** — Add `plantuml_server_url` to settings defaults (NOT a separate settings_service.py)\n    54→7. **Tests** — Cover all new renderers, PUT endpoint, security\n    55→\n    56→---\n    57→\n    58→## Phase 1: Schema & Backend Foundation\n    59→\n    60→**Priority:** HIGH — All other phases depend on this\n    61→**Estimated Complexity:** Low\n    62→**Files:** 5 modified, 0 created\n    63→\n    64→### 1.1 Extend arch-schema.json Type Enum\n    65→\n    66→**File:** `vista/templates/arch-schema.json`\n    67→**Line:** 29\n    68→\n    69→Change:\n    70→```json\n    71→\"enum\": [\"mermaid\", \"drawio\"]\n    72→```\n    73→To:\n    74→```json\n    75→\"enum\": [\"mermaid\", \"drawio\", \"plantuml\", \"d2\", \"graphviz\", \"markdown\"]\n    76→```\n    77→\n    78→No other schema changes needed — `diagramType` enum already has `\"custom\"` as a catch-all for non-Mermaid diagrams. The `category` field is already optional with `architecture` and `tdd` values.\n    79→\n    80→### 1.2 Add write_arch_file() to ProgressService\n    81→\n    82→**File:** `vista/server/services/progress_service.py`\n    83→**Insert after:** `read_arch_file()` method (line 97)\n    84→\n    85→```python\n    86→@staticmethod\n    87→def write_arch_file(project_path: str, feature_name: str, filename: str, content: str) -> bool:\n    88→    \"\"\"Write content to a diagram file in arch/ with path traversal prevention.\n    89→\n    90→    Only allows writing to files with extensions: .md\n    91→    Returns True on success, False on validation failure.\n    92→    \"\"\"\n    93→    WRITABLE_EXTENSIONS = {\".md\"}\n    94→\n    95→    safe_name = Path(filename).name\n    96→    if safe_name != filename or \"..\" in filename:\n    97→        return False\n    98→\n    99→    if Path(safe_name).suffix not in WRITABLE_EXTENSIONS:\n   100→        return False\n   101→\n   102→    arch_dir = Path(project_path) / \".vista\" / \"features\" / feature_name / \"arch\"\n   103→    target = arch_dir / safe_name\n   104→\n   105→    try:\n   106→        target.resolve().relative_to(arch_dir.resolve())\n   107→    except ValueError:\n   108→        return False\n   109→\n   110→    if not arch_dir.exists():\n   111→        return False\n   112→\n   113→    target.write_text(content, encoding=\"utf-8\")\n   114→    return True\n   115→```\n   116→\n   117→**Key decisions:**\n   118→- **Writable extensions restricted to `.md` only** — Diagram files (.mmd, .puml, .d2, .dot, .drawio) are NOT writable through this API. Only markdown documentation files are editable inline.\n   119→- **Same path traversal protection pattern** as existing `read_arch_file()` (lines 80-92).\n   120→- **File must be in an existing arch/ directory** — won't create directories.\n   121→\n   122→### 1.3 Add PUT Endpoint for File Writing\n   123→\n   124→**File:** `vista/server/routes/architecture.py`\n   125→**Insert after:** `get_arch_file()` function (line 48)\n   126→\n   127→```python\n   128→from pydantic import BaseModel\n   129→\n   130→class FileContent(BaseModel):\n   131→    content: str\n   132→\n   133→@router.put(\"/api/projects/{project_id}/features/{feature_name}/arch/{filename}\")\n   134→async def put_arch_file(project_id: str, feature_name: str, filename: str, body: FileContent):\n   135→    \"\"\"Write content to a markdown file in arch/.\"\"\"\n   136→    project = ProjectService.get_by_id(project_id)\n   137→    if not project:\n   138→        raise HTTPException(status_code=404, detail=\"Project not found\")\n   139→\n   140→    success = ProgressService.write_arch_file(project.path, feature_name, filename, body.content)\n   141→    if not success:\n   142→        raise HTTPException(status_code=400, detail=\"Cannot write to this file\")\n   143→\n   144→    return {\"status\": \"ok\", \"filename\": filename}\n   145→```\n   146→\n   147→**Note:** The `pydantic` import may already exist (check top of file). The `BaseModel` import should be added alongside existing imports if not present.\n   148→\n   149→### 1.4 Update Content-Type Mapping in GET Endpoint\n   150→\n   151→**File:** `vista/server/routes/architecture.py` — `get_arch_file()` function\n   152→**Lines:** 40-46\n   153→\n   154→Replace the current if/elif content-type logic:\n   155→```python\n   156→if filename.endswith(\".mmd\"):\n   157→    media_type = \"text/plain\"\n   158→elif filename.endswith(\".drawio\"):\n   159→    media_type = \"application/xml\"\n   160→else:\n   161→    media_type = \"text/plain\"\n   162→```\n   163→\n   164→With a dictionary-based lookup:\n   165→```python\n   166→ext = filename.rsplit(\".\", 1)[-1] if \".\" in filename else \"\"\n   167→CONTENT_TYPES = {\n   168→    \"mmd\": \"text/plain\",\n   169→    \"drawio\": \"application/xml\",\n   170→    \"puml\": \"text/plain\",\n   171→    \"d2\": \"text/plain\",\n   172→    \"dot\": \"text/plain\",\n   173→    \"md\": \"text/markdown\",\n   174→}\n   175→media_type = CONTENT_TYPES.get(ext, \"text/plain\")\n   176→```\n   177→\n   178→### 1.5 Add PlantUML Server URL to Settings\n   179→\n   180→**File:** `vista/server/config.py`\n   181→\n   182→The settings system uses `config.py` with defaults dicts and a `load_settings()` / `save_*()` pattern. Add a new section for diagram settings:\n   183→\n   184→```python\n   185→_DIAGRAM_DEFAULTS = {\n   186→    \"plantuml_server_url\": \"https://www.plantuml.com/plantuml\",\n   187→}\n   188→\n   189→def get_diagram_settings() -> dict:\n   190→    \"\"\"Return merged diagram settings with defaults applied.\"\"\"\n   191→    raw = load_settings().get(\"diagrams\", {})\n   192→    if not isinstance(raw, dict):\n   193→        raw = {}\n   194→    return _merge_dicts(_DIAGRAM_DEFAULTS, raw)\n   195→```\n   196→\n   197→**Also add:** A helper function or use `get_diagram_settings()` in the architecture page route to pass the PlantUML URL to the template.\n   198→\n   199→**Settings file effect:** When `~/.vista/settings.json` contains no `diagrams` section, the default URL (`https://www.plantuml.com/plantuml`) is used. Users can override by adding:\n   200→```json\n   201→{\n   202→  \"diagrams\": {\n   203→    \"plantuml_server_url\": \"http://localhost:8080/plantuml\"\n   204→  }\n   205→}\n   206→```\n   207→\n   208→### 1.6 Extend Diagram Watcher Extensions\n   209→\n   210→**File:** `vista/server/services/diagram_watcher.py`\n   211→\n   212→**Change 1:** Update `WATCH_EXTENSIONS` in BOTH locations (lines 26 and 124):\n   213→```python\n   214→WATCH_EXTENSIONS = {\".mmd\", \".drawio\", \".puml\", \".d2\", \".dot\", \".md\"}\n   215→```\n   216→\n   217→**Change 2:** Add file-type detection by extension (new function):\n   218→```python\n   219→EXT_TO_TYPE = {\n   220→    \".mmd\": \"mermaid\",\n   221→    \".drawio\": \"drawio\",\n   222→    \".puml\": \"plantuml\",\n   223→    \".d2\": \"d2\",\n   224→    \".dot\": \"graphviz\",\n   225→    \".md\": \"markdown\",\n   226→}\n   227→\n   228→def _detect_file_type(path: Path) -> str:\n   229→    \"\"\"Detect diagram type from file extension.\"\"\"\n   230→    return EXT_TO_TYPE.get(path.suffix.lower(), \"mermaid\")\n   231→```\n   232→\n   233→**Change 3:** Update `_update_manifest_sync()` (lines 232-256) to use `_detect_file_type()` for the `type` field. For non-mermaid formats, set `diagramType: \"custom\"`. For mermaid files, continue using `_detect_diagram_type()` for the subtype.\n   234→\n   235→```python\n   236→# In _update_manifest_sync():\n   237→for f in sorted(arch_dir.iterdir()):\n   238→    if f.suffix in EXT_TO_TYPE and not f.name.startswith(\"_\"):\n   239→        file_type = _detect_file_type(f)\n   240→        diagram_type = _detect_diagram_type(f) if file_type == \"mermaid\" else \"custom\"\n   241→        entry = {\n   242→            \"name\": f.stem.replace(\"-\", \" \").replace(\"_\", \" \").title(),\n   243→            \"file\": f.name,\n   244→            \"type\": file_type,\n   245→            \"diagramType\": diagram_type,\n   246→            \"description\": f\"Auto-detected {file_type} diagram\",\n   247→        }\n   248→        diagrams.append(entry)\n   249→```\n   250→\n   251→### Acceptance Criteria (Phase 1)\n   252→\n   253→- [ ] `arch-schema.json` validates manifests with all 6 type values\n   254→- [ ] `PUT /api/.../arch/{filename}` writes `.md` files successfully\n   255→- [ ] `PUT /api/.../arch/{filename}` returns 400 for non-`.md` files\n   256→- [ ] `PUT /api/.../arch/{filename}` blocks path traversal attempts\n   257→- [ ] `GET /api/.../arch/{filename}` returns correct Content-Type for all 6 extensions\n   258→- [ ] Diagram watcher detects changes in all 6 file types\n   259→- [ ] Manifest auto-update correctly identifies file types by extension\n   260→- [ ] `plantuml_server_url` available via `config.get_diagram_settings()`\n   261→\n   262→---\n   263→\n   264→## Phase 2: Client-Side Renderer Infrastructure\n   265→\n   266→**Priority:** HIGH — Core rendering dispatch\n   267→**Depends on:** Phase 1\n   268→**Estimated Complexity:** Medium\n   269→**Files:** 1 modified (architecture.html), CDN scripts added\n   270→\n   271→### 2.1 Refactor Renderer Dispatch\n   272→\n   273→**File:** `vista/server/views/architecture.html`\n   274→**Replace:** `renderDiagramContent()` function (lines 1288-1311)\n   275→\n   276→Currently checks `filename.endsWith('.mmd')` and falls back to `<pre>`. Refactor to a renderer map:\n   277→\n   278→```javascript\n   279→const RENDERERS = {\n   280→    mermaid:  renderMermaid,\n   281→    plantuml: renderPlantUML,\n   282→    d2:       renderD2,\n   283→    graphviz: renderGraphviz,\n   284→    drawio:   renderDrawio,\n   285→    markdown: renderMarkdown,\n   286→};\n   287→\n   288→async function renderDiagramContent(el, filename, content, idx, diagramType) {\n   289→    // diagramType is the 'type' field from manifest (mermaid, plantuml, etc.)\n   290→    const renderer = RENDERERS[diagramType];\n   291→    if (renderer) {\n   292→        return renderer(el, content, idx, filename);\n   293→    }\n   294→    // Unknown type fallback\n   295→    el.innerHTML = `<pre class=\"text-gray-400 text-xs whitespace-pre-wrap\">${escapeHtml(content)}</pre>`;\n   296→}\n   297→```\n   298→\n   299→**Critical change:** `loadDiagrams()` must pass the manifest `type` field to `renderDiagramContent()`. Currently only passes filename/content/idx. Add `diagram.type` as 5th parameter.\n   300→\n   301→### 2.2 Mermaid Renderer (Extract from existing)\n   302→\n   303→Extract the existing mermaid logic (lines 1289-1307) into a standalone function:\n   304→\n   305→```javascript\n   306→async function renderMermaid(el, content, idx, filename) {\n   307→    try {\n   308→        const id = `mermaid-svg-${idx}-${++mermaidCounter}`;\n   309→        const { svg } = await mermaid.render(id, content);\n   310→        el.innerHTML = svg;\n   311→        // Existing node click handlers...\n   312→        el.querySelectorAll('.node').forEach(node => {\n   313→            node.style.cursor = 'pointer';\n   314→            node.addEventListener('click', (e) => {\n   315→                e.stopPropagation();\n   316→                toggleNodeSelection(node, idx);\n   317→            });\n   318→        });\n   319→        reapplySelections(idx);\n   320→    } catch (e) {\n   321→        el.innerHTML = `<pre class=\"text-yellow-400 text-xs whitespace-pre-wrap\">Mermaid parse error:\\n${e.message || e}\\n\\n${content}</pre>`;\n   322→    }\n   323→}\n   324→```\n   325→\n   326→### 2.3 PlantUML Renderer\n   327→\n   328→**CDN dependency:** `plantuml-encoder` v1.4.0 (~10KB minified)\n   329→```html\n   330→<script src=\"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/plantuml-encoder@1.4.0/dist/plantuml-encoder.min.js\"></script>\n   331→```\n   332→\n   333→**Template variable needed:** Pass `PLANTUML_SERVER_URL` from server context.\n   334→\n   335→**Implementation:**\n   336→```javascript\n   337→async function renderPlantUML(el, content, idx, filename) {\n   338→    try {\n   339→        const encoded = plantumlEncoder.encode(content);\n   340→        const svgUrl = `${PLANTUML_SERVER_URL}/svg/${encoded}`;\n   341→        const resp = await fetch(svgUrl);\n   342→        if (!resp.ok) throw new Error(`PlantUML server error: ${resp.status}`);\n   343→        const svg = await resp.text();\n   344→        el.innerHTML = svg;\n   345→    } catch (err) {\n   346→        el.innerHTML = `<div class=\"diagram-error\">\n   347→            <p class=\"text-yellow-400 text-sm mb-2\">PlantUML render error: ${escapeHtml(err.message)}</p>\n   348→            <pre class=\"text-gray-400 text-xs whitespace-pre-wrap\">${escapeHtml(content)}</pre>\n   349→        </div>`;\n   350→    }\n   351→}\n   352→```\n   353→\n   354→**Error handling:**\n   355→- Server unreachable → Show error message + raw source as fallback\n   356→- Invalid syntax → PlantUML server returns an error image; show the raw source too\n   357→\n   358→### 2.4 D2 Renderer\n   359→\n   360→**Dependency status:** `@terrastruct/d2` does NOT have a well-known browser-compatible WASM build available on CDN. After research:\n   361→\n   362→- **d2 official repo** (`terrastruct/d2`) is a Go binary, no WASM distribution\n   363→- **No `@anthropic-ai/d2-wasm`** package exists on npm\n   364→- **Kroki** is a self-hosted diagram server that supports D2 (like PlantUML server)\n   365→\n   366→**Revised approach — Server-side rendering via Kroki or raw source fallback:**\n   367→\n   368→```javascript\n   369→async function renderD2(el, content, idx, filename) {\n   370→    // Attempt 1: If a Kroki server is configured, render via server\n   371→    if (window.KROKI_SERVER_URL) {\n   372→        try {\n   373→            const resp = await fetch(`${KROKI_SERVER_URL}/d2/svg`, {\n   374→                method: 'POST',\n   375→                headers: { 'Content-Type': 'text/plain' },\n   376→                body: content,\n   377→            });\n   378→            if (resp.ok) {\n   379→                el.innerHTML = await resp.text();\n   380→                return;\n   381→            }\n   382→        } catch (_) { /* fall through */ }\n   383→    }\n   384→    // Fallback: Syntax-highlighted raw source\n   385→    el.innerHTML = `<div class=\"diagram-raw-source\">\n   386→        <p class=\"text-blue-400 text-sm mb-2\">D2 diagram (raw source — install Kroki for live rendering)</p>\n   387→        <pre class=\"text-gray-300 text-xs whitespace-pre-wrap\">${escapeHtml(content)}</pre>\n   388→    </div>`;\n   389→}\n   390→```\n   391→\n   392→**Decision:** D2 rendering ships as raw-source-with-syntax-hint initially. Kroki integration (optional) is documented but not required. This avoids a hard dependency on a non-existent WASM package.\n   393→\n   394→**Future enhancement:** If `@anthropic-ai/d2-wasm` or similar becomes available, swap in client-side rendering.\n   395→\n   396→### 2.5 Graphviz Renderer\n   397→\n   398→**CDN dependency:** `@viz-js/viz` v3 — well-established WASM package (~2.5MB)\n   399→\n   400→The package provides a standalone build that works in browsers. Load lazily:\n   401→\n   402→```javascript\n   403→let vizInstance = null;\n   404→\n   405→async function loadViz() {\n   406→    if (vizInstance) return vizInstance;\n   407→    // Dynamic script load\n   408→    if (!window.Viz) {\n   409→        await new Promise((resolve, reject) => {\n   410→            const script = document.createElement('script');\n   411→            script.src = 'https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/@viz-js/viz@3.11.0/lib/viz-standalone.js';\n   412→            script.onload = resolve;\n   413→            script.onerror = reject;\n   414→            document.head.appendChild(script);\n   415→        });\n   416→    }\n   417→    vizInstance = await Viz.instance();\n   418→    return vizInstance;\n   419→}\n   420→\n   421→async function renderGraphviz(el, content, idx, filename) {\n   422→    try {\n   423→        const viz = await loadViz();\n   424→        const svg = viz.renderSVGElement(content);\n   425→        el.innerHTML = '';\n   426→        el.appendChild(svg);\n   427→    } catch (err) {\n   428→        el.innerHTML = `<div class=\"diagram-error\">\n   429→            <p class=\"text-yellow-400 text-sm mb-2\">Graphviz render error: ${escapeHtml(err.message)}</p>\n   430→            <pre class=\"text-gray-400 text-xs whitespace-pre-wrap\">${escapeHtml(content)}</pre>\n   431→        </div>`;\n   432→    }\n   433→}\n   434→```\n   435→\n   436→**Engine selection:** Default to `dot` layout engine. Graphviz supports `dot`, `neato`, `fdp`, `sfdp`, `circo`, `twopi`, `osage`, `patchwork`. Could expose engine via manifest `layoutEngine` field in future — not in scope now.\n   437→\n   438→### 2.6 Draw.io Renderer\n   439→\n   440→**Current state:** Falls through to `<pre>` tag with escaped XML content. No rendering.\n   441→\n   442→**Implementation using Draw.io viewer iframe:**\n   443→```javascript\n   444→function renderDrawio(el, content, idx, filename) {\n   445→    try {\n   446→        // Use postMessage API for large files (URL encoding may exceed limits)\n   447→        const iframe = document.createElement('iframe');\n   448→        iframe.style.width = '100%';\n   449→        iframe.style.height = '500px';\n   450→        iframe.style.border = 'none';\n   451→        iframe.style.borderRadius = '8px';\n   452→        iframe.setAttribute('sandbox', 'allow-scripts allow-same-origin');\n   453→\n   454→        // Base64 encode to avoid URL length limits\n   455→        const b64 = btoa(unescape(encodeURIComponent(content)));\n   456→        iframe.src = `https://viewer.diagrams.net/?highlight=0000ff&nav=1&title=${encodeURIComponent(filename)}#R${b64}`;\n   457→\n   458→        el.innerHTML = '';\n   459→        el.appendChild(iframe);\n   460→    } catch (err) {\n   461→        el.innerHTML = `<div class=\"diagram-error\">\n   462→            <p class=\"text-yellow-400 text-sm mb-2\">Draw.io render error: ${escapeHtml(err.message)}</p>\n   463→            <pre class=\"text-gray-400 text-xs whitespace-pre-wrap\">${escapeHtml(content)}</pre>\n   464→        </div>`;\n   465→    }\n   466→}\n   467→```\n   468→\n   469→**Risk:** Very large `.drawio` files may exceed URL limits even with base64 encoding. For MVP, this approach is acceptable. For large files, the `postMessage` API approach can be added later.\n   470→\n   471→### 2.7 Markdown Renderer\n   472→\n   473→**Library:** `marked.js` — **already loaded** in `architecture.html` (line 7). No additional CDN script needed.\n   474→\n   475→```javascript\n   476→function renderMarkdown(el, content, idx, filename) {\n   477→    try {\n   478→        const html = marked.parse(content);\n   479→        el.innerHTML = `<div class=\"markdown-content\">${html}</div>`;\n   480→        // Store original content for edit mode\n   481→        el.dataset.rawContent = content;\n   482→        el.dataset.filename = filename;\n   483→        el.dataset.idx = idx;\n   484→    } catch (err) {\n   485→        el.innerHTML = `<pre class=\"text-gray-400 text-xs whitespace-pre-wrap\">${escapeHtml(content)}</pre>`;\n   486→    }\n   487→}\n   488→```\n   489→\n   490→### Acceptance Criteria (Phase 2)\n   491→\n   492→- [ ] Mermaid diagrams continue to render correctly (no regression)\n   493→- [ ] PlantUML diagrams render as SVG via server fetch\n   494→- [ ] D2 diagrams show raw source with info message (or Kroki SVG if configured)\n   495→- [ ] Graphviz diagrams render via `@viz-js/viz` WASM\n   496→- [ ] Draw.io diagrams render in iframe (not raw XML)\n   497→- [ ] Markdown files render as formatted HTML via `marked.js`\n   498→- [ ] Each renderer shows error + raw source on failure\n   499→- [ ] WASM module (Graphviz) loads lazily\n   500→- [ ] PlantUML encoder loads eagerly (small, ~10KB)\n   501→\n   502→---\n   503→\n   504→## Phase 3: Markdown Inline Editor\n   505→\n   506→**Priority:** HIGH — Key new user interaction\n   507→**Depends on:** Phase 1 (PUT endpoint), Phase 2 (markdown renderer)\n   508→**Estimated Complexity:** Medium-High\n   509→**Files:** 1 modified (architecture.html), 1 modified (arch-chat.css or inline styles)\n   510→\n   511→### 3.1 Edit Button on Markdown Cards\n   512→\n   513→When building diagram cards in JavaScript (NOT Jinja2 — cards are built client-side), check the diagram type from the manifest entry:\n   514→\n   515→```javascript\n   516→function buildDiagramCard(diagram, idx) {\n   517→    // ... existing card structure ...\n   518→    const editButton = diagram.type === 'markdown'\n   519→        ? `<button class=\"md-edit-btn\" onclick=\"toggleMarkdownEdit(${idx})\" title=\"Edit markdown\">✎</button>`\n   520→        : '';\n   521→    // Insert into card header alongside existing zoom controls\n   522→}\n   523→```\n   524→\n   525→**Placement:** In the diagram card header template area of `architecture.html` — identify where card headers are constructed (likely near line 1016-1041) and add the edit button conditionally.\n   526→\n   527→### 3.2 Edit Mode State Machine\n   528→\n   529→**States:** `view` → `editing` → `saving` → `view`\n   530→\n   531→```javascript\n   532→const markdownEditState = {};  // idx -> { editing: bool, saving: bool, originalContent: string }\n   533→\n   534→function toggleMarkdownEdit(idx) {\n   535→    const state = markdownEditState[idx] || { editing: false };\n   536→    if (state.editing) {\n   537→        cancelMarkdownEdit(idx);\n   538→    } else {\n   539→        enterMarkdownEdit(idx);\n   540→    }\n   541→}\n   542→\n   543→function enterMarkdownEdit(idx) {\n   544→    const el = document.getElementById(`diagram-viewport-${idx}`);\n   545→    const content = el.dataset.rawContent || diagramContents[DIAGRAMS[idx].file];\n   546→\n   547→    markdownEditState[idx] = { editing: true, saving: false, originalContent: content };\n   548→\n   549→    el.innerHTML = `\n   550→        <div class=\"md-editor-container\">\n   551→            <div class=\"md-editor-toolbar\">\n   552→                <button class=\"md-save-btn\" onclick=\"saveMarkdown(${idx})\" title=\"Save\">✓ Save</button>\n   553→                <button class=\"md-cancel-btn\" onclick=\"cancelMarkdownEdit(${idx})\" title=\"Cancel\">✕ Cancel</button>\n   554→                <span class=\"md-save-indicator\" id=\"md-indicator-${idx}\"></span>\n   555→            </div>\n   556→            <textarea class=\"md-editor\" id=\"md-textarea-${idx}\" spellcheck=\"false\">${escapeHtml(content)}</textarea>\n   557→        </div>\n   558→    `;\n   559→\n   560→    const textarea = document.getElementById(`md-textarea-${idx}`);\n   561→    textarea.focus();\n   562→    autoResizeTextarea(textarea);\n   563→    textarea.addEventListener('input', () => autoResizeTextarea(textarea));\n   564→\n   565→    updateEditButton(idx, true);\n   566→}\n   567→\n   568→function cancelMarkdownEdit(idx) {\n   569→    const state = markdownEditState[idx];\n   570→    if (!state) return;\n   571→\n   572→    const el = document.getElementById(`diagram-viewport-${idx}`);\n   573→    renderMarkdown(el, state.originalContent, idx, DIAGRAMS[idx].file);\n   574→\n   575→    markdownEditState[idx] = { editing: false };\n   576→    updateEditButton(idx, false);\n   577→}\n   578→\n   579→async function saveMarkdown(idx) {\n   580→    const state = markdownEditState[idx];\n   581→    if (!state || state.saving) return;\n   582→\n   583→    const textarea = document.getElementById(`md-textarea-${idx}`);\n   584→    const newContent = textarea.value;\n   585→    const filename = DIAGRAMS[idx].file;\n   586→    const indicator = document.getElementById(`md-indicator-${idx}`);\n   587→\n   588→    state.saving = true;\n   589→    indicator.textContent = 'Saving...';\n   590→    indicator.className = 'md-save-indicator saving';\n   591→\n   592→    try {\n   593→        const resp = await fetch(\n   594→            `/api/projects/${PROJECT_ID}/features/${FEATURE_NAME}/arch/${filename}`,\n   595→            {\n   596→                method: 'PUT',\n   597→                headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },\n   598→                body: JSON.stringify({ content: newContent }),\n   599→            }\n   600→        );\n   601→\n   602→        if (!resp.ok) throw new Error(`Save failed: ${resp.status}`);\n   603→\n   604→        indicator.textContent = 'Saved!';\n   605→        indicator.className = 'md-save-indicator saved';\n   606→\n   607→        // Update stored content\n   608→        diagramContents[filename] = newContent;\n   609→\n   610→        // Return to view mode after brief success indicator\n   611→        setTimeout(() => {\n   612→            const el = document.getElementById(`diagram-viewport-${idx}`);\n   613→            renderMarkdown(el, newContent, idx, filename);\n   614→            markdownEditState[idx] = { editing: false };\n   615→            updateEditButton(idx, false);\n   616→        }, 800);\n   617→\n   618→    } catch (err) {\n   619→        indicator.textContent = `Error: ${err.message}`;\n   620→        indicator.className = 'md-save-indicator error';\n   621→        state.saving = false;\n   622→    }\n   623→}\n   624→\n   625→function autoResizeTextarea(textarea) {\n   626→    textarea.style.height = 'auto';\n   627→    textarea.style.height = Math.max(200, textarea.scrollHeight) + 'px';\n   628→}\n   629→\n   630→function updateEditButton(idx, isEditing) {\n   631→    const btn = document.querySelector(`[data-edit-idx=\"${idx}\"]`);\n   632→    if (btn) {\n   633→        btn.textContent = isEditing ? '✕' : '✎';\n   634→        btn.title = isEditing ? 'Cancel editing' : 'Edit markdown';\n   635→    }\n   636→}\n   637→```\n   638→\n   639→### 3.3 Keyboard Shortcuts\n   640→\n   641→```javascript\n   642→document.addEventListener('keydown', (e) => {\n   643→    for (const [idx, state] of Object.entries(markdownEditState)) {\n   644→        if (state.editing) {\n   645→            if ((e.ctrlKey || e.metaKey) && e.key === 's') {\n   646→                e.preventDefault();\n   647→                saveMarkdown(parseInt(idx));\n   648→            } else if (e.key === 'Escape') {\n   649→                e.preventDefault();\n   650→                cancelMarkdownEdit(parseInt(idx));\n   651→            }\n   652→        }\n   653→    }\n   654→});\n   655→```\n   656→\n   657→### 3.4 Editor CSS Styles\n   658→\n   659→**File:** `vista/server/views/static/arch-chat.css` (or inline in architecture.html `<style>` block)\n   660→\n   661→```css\n   662→.md-editor-container {\n   663→    display: flex;\n   664→    flex-direction: column;\n   665→    height: 100%;\n   666→    min-height: 200px;\n   667→}\n   668→\n   669→.md-editor-toolbar {\n   670→    display: flex;\n   671→    align-items: center;\n   672→    gap: 8px;\n   673→    padding: 8px 12px;\n   674→    background: var(--surface-2, #1e293b);\n   675→    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border, #334155);\n   676→}\n   677→\n   678→.md-editor {\n   679→    flex: 1;\n   680→    resize: vertical;\n   681→    min-height: 200px;\n   682→    padding: 16px;\n   683→    font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', 'Fira Code', monospace;\n   684→    font-size: 14px;\n   685→    line-height: 1.6;\n   686→    background: var(--surface-1, #0f172a);\n   687→    color: var(--text-primary, #e2e8f0);\n   688→    border: none;\n   689→    outline: none;\n   690→}\n   691→\n   692→.md-edit-btn {\n   693→    cursor: pointer;\n   694→    padding: 4px 8px;\n   695→    border-radius: 4px;\n   696→    opacity: 0.6;\n   697→    transition: opacity 0.2s;\n   698→}\n   699→.md-edit-btn:hover { opacity: 1; }\n   700→\n   701→.md-save-btn { color: #4ade80; cursor: pointer; }\n   702→.md-cancel-btn { color: #f87171; cursor: pointer; }\n   703→.md-save-indicator.saving { color: #facc15; }\n   704→.md-save-indicator.saved { color: #4ade80; }\n   705→.md-save-indicator.error { color: #f87171; }\n   706→\n   707→.markdown-content {\n   708→    padding: 16px;\n   709→    line-height: 1.7;\n   710→}\n   711→.markdown-content h1, .markdown-content h2, .markdown-content h3 {\n   712→    margin-top: 1.5em;\n   713→    margin-bottom: 0.5em;\n   714→}\n   715→.markdown-content pre {\n   716→    background: var(--surface-2, #1e293b);\n   717→    padding: 12px;\n   718→    border-radius: 6px;\n   719→    overflow-x: auto;\n   720→}\n   721→.markdown-content code {\n   722→    background: var(--surface-2, #1e293b);\n   723→    padding: 2px 6px;\n   724→    border-radius: 3px;\n   725→    font-size: 0.9em;\n   726→}\n   727→.markdown-content table {\n   728→    border-collapse: collapse;\n   729→    width: 100%;\n   730→}\n   731→.markdown-content th, .markdown-content td {\n   732→    border: 1px solid var(--border, #334155);\n   733→    padding: 8px 12px;\n   734→    text-align: left;\n   735→}\n   736→```\n   737→\n   738→### Acceptance Criteria (Phase 3)\n   739→\n   740→- [ ] Markdown files render as formatted HTML with GFM support (tables, code blocks, task lists)\n   741→- [ ] Edit button appears only on markdown-type diagram cards\n   742→- [ ] Clicking edit switches to textarea with raw content\n   743→- [ ] Save writes content to disk via PUT API and returns to rendered view\n   744→- [ ] Cancel discards changes and returns to rendered view\n   745→- [ ] Save indicator shows progress (saving → saved → hidden)\n   746→- [ ] Save failure shows error message, does not lose edits\n   747→- [ ] Ctrl+S / Cmd+S saves, Escape cancels\n   748→- [ ] Content stored in `diagramContents` is updated after successful save\n   749→\n   750→---\n   751→\n   752→## Phase 4: Template & Watcher Integration\n   753→\n   754→**Priority:** MEDIUM\n   755→**Depends on:** Phases 1-3\n   756→**Estimated Complexity:** Low-Medium\n   757→**Files:** 2 modified (architecture.html, architecture.py route)\n   758→\n   759→### 4.1 Pass Manifest Type to Renderers\n   760→\n   761→**File:** `vista/server/views/architecture.html`\n   762→\n   763→Update `loadDiagrams()` to pass the manifest `type` field:\n   764→\n   765→```javascript\n   766→async function loadDiagrams() {\n   767→    for (let i = 0; i < DIAGRAMS.length; i++) {\n   768→        const diagram = DIAGRAMS[i];\n   769→        const resp = await fetch(`/api/projects/${PROJECT_ID}/features/${FEATURE_NAME}/arch/${diagram.file}`);\n   770→        const content = await resp.text();\n   771→        diagramContents[diagram.file] = content;\n   772→\n   773→        const el = document.getElementById(`diagram-viewport-${i}`);\n   774→        renderDiagramContent(el, diagram.file, content, i, diagram.type);  // 5th arg: type\n   775→    }\n   776→}\n   777→```\n   778→\n   779→### 4.2 Conditionally Show Edit Button in Card Header\n   780→\n   781→When building diagram cards (JavaScript), check the diagram type:\n   782→\n   783→```javascript\n   784→// Inside card header construction\n   785→const editButton = diagram.type === 'markdown'\n   786→    ? `<button class=\"md-edit-btn\" data-edit-idx=\"${idx}\" onclick=\"toggleMarkdownEdit(${idx})\" title=\"Edit\">✎</button>`\n   787→    : '';\n   788→```\n   789→\n   790→### 4.3 CDN Script Loading\n   791→\n   792→**File:** `vista/server/views/architecture.html` — `<head>` section\n   793→\n   794→Add after existing mermaid.js and marked.js CDN lines:\n   795→\n   796→```html\n   797→<!-- PlantUML encoder (small, ~10KB) — loaded eagerly -->\n   798→<script src=\"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/plantuml-encoder@1.4.0/dist/plantuml-encoder.min.js\"></script>\n   799→\n   800→<!-- @viz-js/viz loaded lazily by renderGraphviz() — no eager script needed -->\n   801→<!-- Draw.io viewer loaded as iframe — no script needed -->\n   802→```\n   803→\n   804→### 4.4 PlantUML Server URL Injection\n   805→\n   806→**File:** `vista/server/routes/architecture.py` — `architecture_viewer_page()` (line 51-66)\n   807→\n   808→Add the PlantUML server URL to the template context:\n   809→\n   810→```python\n   811→from server.config import get_diagram_settings\n   812→\n   813→@router.get(\"/project/{project_id}/arch/{feature_name}\", response_class=HTMLResponse)\n   814→async def architecture_viewer_page(request: Request, project_id: str, feature_name: str):\n   815→    # ... existing code ...\n   816→    diagram_settings = get_diagram_settings()\n   817→    plantuml_url = diagram_settings.get(\"plantuml_server_url\", \"https://www.plantuml.com/plantuml\")\n   818→    return templates.TemplateResponse(\"architecture.html\", {\n   819→        \"request\": request,\n   820→        # ... existing context vars ...\n   821→        \"plantuml_url\": plantuml_url,\n   822→    })\n   823→```\n   824→\n   825→And in the template:\n   826→```html\n   827→<script>\n   828→    const PLANTUML_SERVER_URL = {{ plantuml_url | tojson }};\n   829→</script>\n   830→```\n   831→\n   832→### Acceptance Criteria (Phase 4)\n   833→\n   834→- [ ] All 6 diagram types dispatch to their correct renderer via `diagram.type`\n   835→- [ ] Edit button only appears on markdown cards\n   836→- [ ] PlantUML server URL passed from settings to frontend\n   837→- [ ] PlantUML encoder CDN script loaded\n   838→- [ ] Graphviz WASM loads lazily on first Graphviz diagram\n   839→\n   840→---\n   841→\n   842→## Phase 5: Tests\n   843→\n   844→**Priority:** HIGH — Must validate security and correctness\n   845→**Depends on:** Phases 1-4\n   846→**Estimated Complexity:** Medium\n   847→**Files:** 2 modified (test_architecture.py, test_diagram_watcher.py)\n   848→\n   849→### 5.1 PUT Endpoint Tests\n   850→\n   851→**File:** `vista/tests/test_architecture.py`\n   852→**Add class:** `TestArchWriteAPI` (after existing `TestArchitectureAPI` at line 227)\n   853→\n   854→```python\n   855→class TestArchWriteAPI:\n   856→    def test_put_markdown_file_success(self, api_env):\n   857→        \"\"\"PUT .md file writes content and returns 200.\"\"\"\n   858→\n   859→    def test_put_non_markdown_file_rejected(self, api_env):\n   860→        \"\"\"PUT .mmd file returns 400.\"\"\"\n   861→\n   862→    def test_put_path_traversal_blocked(self, api_env):\n   863→        \"\"\"PUT ../../evil.md returns 400.\"\"\"\n   864→\n   865→    def test_put_dotdot_in_filename(self, api_env):\n   866→        \"\"\"PUT with '..' anywhere in filename returns 400.\"\"\"\n   867→\n   868→    def test_put_project_not_found(self, api_env):\n   869→        \"\"\"PUT to nonexistent project returns 404.\"\"\"\n   870→\n   871→    def test_put_no_arch_directory(self, api_env):\n   872→        \"\"\"PUT to feature without arch/ returns 400.\"\"\"\n   873→\n   874→    def test_put_verify_file_written(self, api_env):\n   875→        \"\"\"After successful PUT, GET returns the new content.\"\"\"\n   876→```\n   877→\n   878→### 5.2 ProgressService Write Tests\n   879→\n   880→**File:** `vista/tests/test_architecture.py`\n   881→**Add class:** `TestProgressServiceWrite` (after existing `TestProgressServiceArch` at line 318)\n   882→\n   883→```python\n   884→class TestProgressServiceWrite:\n   885→    def test_write_arch_file_md_success(self, tmp_path):\n   886→        \"\"\"write_arch_file() writes .md content to arch/.\"\"\"\n   887→\n   888→    def test_write_arch_file_mmd_rejected(self, tmp_path):\n   889→        \"\"\"write_arch_file() rejects .mmd files.\"\"\"\n   890→\n   891→    def test_write_arch_file_puml_rejected(self, tmp_path):\n   892→        \"\"\"write_arch_file() rejects .puml files.\"\"\"\n   893→\n   894→    def test_write_arch_file_path_traversal(self, tmp_path):\n   895→        \"\"\"write_arch_file() blocks ../evil path.\"\"\"\n   896→\n   897→    def test_write_arch_file_no_arch_dir(self, tmp_path):\n   898→        \"\"\"write_arch_file() returns False when arch/ doesn't exist.\"\"\"\n   899→\n   900→    def test_write_arch_file_overwrites_existing(self, tmp_path):\n   901→        \"\"\"write_arch_file() overwrites an existing .md file.\"\"\"\n   902→```\n   903→\n   904→### 5.3 Extended Schema Validation Tests\n   905→\n   906→**File:** `vista/tests/test_architecture.py`\n   907→**Add to existing `TestSchemaValidation` class** (line 320)\n   908→\n   909→```python\n   910→def test_arch_schema_accepts_plantuml_type(self):\n   911→def test_arch_schema_accepts_d2_type(self):\n   912→def test_arch_schema_accepts_graphviz_type(self):\n   913→def test_arch_schema_accepts_markdown_type(self):\n   914→# Note: test_arch_schema_rejects_invalid_type already exists (line 416)\n   915→```\n   916→\n   917→### 5.4 Content-Type Tests\n   918→\n   919→**File:** `vista/tests/test_architecture.py`\n   920→**Add class:** `TestContentTypes`\n   921→\n   922→```python\n   923→class TestContentTypes:\n   924→    def test_get_puml_returns_text_plain(self, api_env):\n   925→    def test_get_d2_returns_text_plain(self, api_env):\n   926→    def test_get_dot_returns_text_plain(self, api_env):\n   927→    def test_get_md_returns_text_markdown(self, api_env):\n   928→```\n   929→\n   930→### 5.5 Diagram Watcher Extension Tests\n   931→\n   932→**File:** `vista/tests/test_diagram_watcher.py`\n   933→**Add class:** `TestExtendedFileTypes` (after existing `TestManifestUpdate` at line 193)\n   934→\n   935→```python\n   936→class TestExtendedFileTypes:\n   937→    def test_watches_puml_files(self):\n   938→        \"\"\"WATCH_EXTENSIONS includes .puml.\"\"\"\n   939→\n   940→    def test_watches_d2_files(self):\n   941→        \"\"\"WATCH_EXTENSIONS includes .d2.\"\"\"\n   942→\n   943→    def test_watches_dot_files(self):\n   944→        \"\"\"WATCH_EXTENSIONS includes .dot.\"\"\"\n   945→\n   946→    def test_watches_md_files(self):\n   947→        \"\"\"WATCH_EXTENSIONS includes .md.\"\"\"\n   948→\n   949→    def test_detect_file_type_plantuml(self):\n   950→        \"\"\"_detect_file_type() returns 'plantuml' for .puml.\"\"\"\n   951→\n   952→    def test_detect_file_type_d2(self):\n   953→        \"\"\"_detect_file_type() returns 'd2' for .d2.\"\"\"\n   954→\n   955→    def test_detect_file_type_graphviz(self):\n   956→        \"\"\"_detect_file_type() returns 'graphviz' for .dot.\"\"\"\n   957→\n   958→    def test_detect_file_type_markdown(self):\n   959→        \"\"\"_detect_file_type() returns 'markdown' for .md.\"\"\"\n   960→\n   961→    def test_manifest_update_assigns_correct_type_plantuml(self):\n   962→        \"\"\"Manifest update sets type='plantuml' for .puml files.\"\"\"\n   963→\n   964→    def test_manifest_update_assigns_correct_type_markdown(self):\n   965→        \"\"\"Manifest update sets type='markdown' for .md files.\"\"\"\n   966→```\n   967→\n   968→### 5.6 Settings Tests\n   969→\n   970→**File:** `vista/tests/test_architecture.py` (or new `test_config.py` if appropriate)\n   971→\n   972→```python\n   973→class TestDiagramSettings:\n   974→    def test_get_diagram_settings_default(self):\n   975→        \"\"\"Default plantuml_server_url is plantuml.com.\"\"\"\n   976→\n   977→    def test_get_diagram_settings_override(self):\n   978→        \"\"\"Custom plantuml_server_url from settings.json is returned.\"\"\"\n   979→```\n   980→\n   981→### Test Count Summary\n   982→\n   983→| Category | New Tests | Location |\n   984→|----------|-----------|----------|\n   985→| PUT endpoint | 7 | `test_architecture.py` |\n   986→| ProgressService write | 6 | `test_architecture.py` |\n   987→| Schema validation | 4 | `test_architecture.py` |\n   988→| Content types | 4 | `test_architecture.py` |\n   989→| Diagram watcher extensions | 10 | `test_diagram_watcher.py` |\n   990→| Settings | 2 | `test_architecture.py` |\n   991→| **Total new** | **33** | |\n   992→\n   993→### Acceptance Criteria (Phase 5)\n   994→\n   995→- [ ] All PUT endpoint tests pass (including security: path traversal, extension whitelist)\n   996→- [ ] All schema validation tests pass for 6 types\n   997→- [ ] Content-type tests pass for all new extensions\n   998→- [ ] Watcher tests pass for all 6 file types\n   999→- [ ] Settings tests pass for defaults and overrides\n  1000→- [ ] No regressions in existing 53 tests (29 arch + 24 watcher)\n  1001→- [ ] Total test count: ~86 (53 existing + 33 new)\n  1002→\n  1003→---\n  1004→\n  1005→## Phase 6: Documentation & Skill Updates\n  1006→\n  1007→**Priority:** LOW\n  1008→**Depends on:** All prior phases\n  1009→**Estimated Complexity:** Low\n  1010→\n  1011→### 6.1 Update Plan Skill SKILL.md\n  1012→\n  1013→**File:** `vista/skills/plan/SKILL.md`\n  1014→\n  1015→Update Step 3 (architecture generation) to mention all supported formats:\n  1016→- Default: Mermaid (.mmd) for all diagram types\n  1017→- Optional: PlantUML (.puml) for detailed UML class/sequence diagrams\n  1018→- Optional: D2 (.d2) for architecture diagrams (raw source unless Kroki configured)\n  1019→- Optional: Graphviz (.dot) for dependency graphs\n  1020→- Optional: Markdown (.md) for prose documentation (design rationale, ADRs)\n  1021→\n  1022→### 6.2 Update Diagrams Skill\n  1023→\n  1024→**File:** `vista/skills/diagrams/SKILL.md`\n  1025→\n  1026→Document the expanded format support.\n  1027→\n  1028→### 6.3 Update Specs\n  1029→\n  1030→**arch-directory.md:**\n  1031→- Update supported types from `\"mermaid\" | \"drawio\"` to all 6 values\n  1032→- Update data model DiagramEntry type union\n  1033→- Add markdown editing workflow\n  1034→\n  1035→**rendering-pipeline.md:**\n  1036→- Update renderer table to include all 6 renderers\n  1037→- Add CDN dependency table\n  1038→- Document lazy vs eager loading strategy\n  1039→\n  1040→### Acceptance Criteria (Phase 6)\n  1041→\n  1042→- [ ] Plan skill lists all supported formats\n  1043→- [ ] Diagrams skill documents expanded support\n  1044→- [ ] Specs updated to reflect all 6 types\n  1045→- [ ] Renderer table complete in rendering-pipeline.md\n  1046→\n  1047→---\n  1048→\n  1049→## Risk Assessment\n  1050→\n  1051→| Risk | Likelihood | Impact | Mitigation |\n  1052→|------|-----------|--------|------------|\n  1053→| D2 WASM not available as browser-compatible package | **Confirmed** | Low | Ship with raw source display + optional Kroki integration |\n  1054→| PlantUML server rate limiting or network issues | Low | Low | Self-hosted server option in settings; error + raw source fallback |\n  1055→| `@viz-js/viz` WASM too large (>5MB) | Low | Medium | Lazy load only when Graphviz diagram appears; ~2.5MB actual |\n  1056→| Draw.io viewer base64 URL exceeds limits for large files | Medium | Medium | Base64 approach for MVP; postMessage API for future |\n  1057→| Markdown editor unsaved changes lost on navigation | Low | Medium | Add `beforeunload` warning when editing (enhancement) |\n  1058→| `marked.js` XSS via user-edited markdown | Low | High | Use `marked` with default sanitization; content is user-owned files |\n  1059→\n  1060→---\n  1061→\n  1062→## Implementation Order (Recommended)\n  1063→\n  1064→1. **Phase 1** — Backend foundation (schema, PUT endpoint, watcher extensions, settings)\n  1065→2. **Phase 5 partial** — Backend tests for Phase 1 (schema, PUT, watcher, settings) — validate before frontend\n  1066→3. **Phase 2** — Renderer infrastructure (dispatch refactor + all 6 renderers)\n  1067→4. **Phase 3** — Markdown editor (edit mode, save/cancel, keyboard shortcuts)\n  1068→5. **Phase 4** — Template integration (type passing, CDN loading, URL injection)\n  1069→6. **Phase 5 remainder** — Content type tests, integration tests\n  1070→7. **Phase 6** — Documentation\n  1071→\n  1072→**Estimated total:** ~3-4 build iterations\n  1073→\n  1074→---\n  1075→\n  1076→## Files Summary\n  1077→\n  1078→### Files to Modify\n  1079→\n  1080→| File | Changes |\n  1081→|------|---------|\n  1082→| `vista/templates/arch-schema.json` | Extend `type` enum: add `plantuml`, `d2`, `graphviz`, `markdown` (line 29) |\n  1083→| `vista/server/services/progress_service.py` | Add `write_arch_file()` method (after line 97) |\n  1084→| `vista/server/routes/architecture.py` | Add PUT endpoint (after line 48), update content-type mapping (lines 40-46) |\n  1085→| `vista/server/views/architecture.html` | Refactor renderer dispatch (lines 1288-1311), add 5 new renderers, add markdown editor, CDN scripts |\n  1086→| `vista/server/views/static/arch-chat.css` | Add markdown editor + content styles |\n  1087→| `vista/server/services/diagram_watcher.py` | Extend `WATCH_EXTENSIONS` (lines 26, 124), add `_detect_file_type()`, update `_update_manifest_sync()` |\n  1088→| `vista/server/config.py` | Add `_DIAGRAM_DEFAULTS` and `get_diagram_settings()` |\n  1089→| `vista/tests/test_architecture.py` | Add ~23 new tests (PUT, schema, content types, settings) |\n  1090→| `vista/tests/test_diagram_watcher.py` | Add ~10 new tests (extended file types, type detection) |\n  1091→\n  1092→### Files to Create\n  1093→\n  1094→None — all changes are modifications to existing files.\n  1095→\n  1096→### Settings Changes\n  1097→\n  1098→| Setting | Default Value | Location |\n  1099→|---------|--------------|----------|\n  1100→| `diagrams.plantuml_server_url` | `\"https://www.plantuml.com/plantuml\"` | `~/.vista/settings.json` via `config.py` |\n  1101→\n  1102→---\n  1103→\n  1104→## Key Corrections from Iteration 1\n  1105→\n  1106→| # | Iteration 1 Claim | Correction |\n  1107→|---|-------------------|------------|\n  1108→| 1 | \"File: `settings_service.py`\" for settings | **Corrected:** Settings service is `config.py` — no `settings_service.py` exists |\n  1109→| 2 | D2 renders via `@terrastruct/d2` WASM or `@anthropic-ai/d2-wasm` | **Corrected:** Neither package exists. D2 ships as raw source + optional Kroki server |\n  1110→| 3 | `@viz-js/viz` CDN path left unspecified | **Corrected:** `@viz-js/viz@3.11.0/lib/viz-standalone.js` — lazy-loaded script tag |\n  1111→| 4 | `WATCH_EXTENSIONS` referenced once | **Corrected:** Defined in TWO locations (lines 26 and 124) — both must be updated |\n  1112→| 5 | ~20 new tests estimated | **Corrected:** 33 new tests planned (more thorough coverage) |\n  1113→\n  1114→---\n  1115→\n  1116→## Spec Versions\n  1117→\n  1118→| Spec File | Latest Changelog Date | Notes |\n  1119→|-----------|-----------------------|-------|\n  1120→| `specs/arch-directory.md` | 2026-02-15 | `diagramType` enum and category aligned with arch-schema.json |\n  1121→| `specs/rendering-pipeline.md` | 2026-02-15 | Draw.io status clarified, acceptance criteria updated |\n  1122→| `specs/chat-review.md` | 2026-02-15 | Protocol-native streaming alignment |\n  1123→| `specs/migration-cleanup.md` | 2026-02-15 | All acceptance criteria verified complete |\n  1124→| `domain-requirements.md` (Expansion) | 2026-02-15 | Multi-format diagrams, markdown editing, type system updates |\n  1125→"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"371e7b79-44db-4908-8208-61ee911d648c","uuid":"f5367f45-9305-48af-b4a1-6503acb0f5ec","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:/Users/Grove/OneDrive/Documents/PYTHON/claude_plugins/vista-expanded-visualization/.vista/ralph/diagram-repr-spec-planning/IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md","content":"# Implementation Plan: Multi-Format Diagram Support & Markdown Editing\n\n**Status:** PLANNING — Iteration 2 (refined, codebase-verified)\n**Created:** 2026-02-15\n**Updated:** 2026-02-15 (Iteration 2 — settings path fix, CDN verification, precise line refs)\n**Spec Source:** `domain-requirements.md` Expansion section (added 2026-02-15)\n**Parent Feature:** `.vista/features/diagram_representations/`\n\n---\n\n## Context\n\nThe existing diagram_representations feature is largely delivered (Phases 1-4 complete, Phase 5 partial). The domain-requirements.md has been expanded with three new areas:\n\n1. **Multi-Format Rendering** — PlantUML (.puml), D2 (.d2), Graphviz (.dot), Markdown (.md)\n2. **Markdown Inline Editing** — View/edit toggle, save to disk via PUT API, cancel/discard\n3. **Manifest & Type System Updates** — Extended type enum, renderer dispatch, file extension mapping\n\nThis plan covers implementing these expansion requirements on top of the existing codebase.\n\n---\n\n## Current State Assessment (Verified Iteration 2)\n\n### What Exists (Working)\n\n| Component | Status | Location (verified) |\n|-----------|--------|---------------------|\n| Mermaid rendering | Complete | `architecture.html:1288-1307` — `mermaid.render()` |\n| Renderer dispatch | Partial — only `.mmd` check + fallback `<pre>` | `architecture.html:1288-1311` — `renderDiagramContent()` |\n| `_arch.json` schema | `type` enum: `[\"mermaid\", \"drawio\"]` only | `arch-schema.json:29` |\n| Diagram watcher | Watches `.mmd` and `.drawio` only | `diagram_watcher.py:26,124` — `WATCH_EXTENSIONS` (defined twice) |\n| `_detect_diagram_type()` | Parses mermaid subtype from first line of `.mmd` | `diagram_watcher.py:102-118` |\n| Manifest auto-update | Scans `.mmd`/`.drawio` in arch dir, builds `_arch.json` | `diagram_watcher.py:232-256` — `_update_manifest_sync()` |\n| API: GET manifest | Complete | `architecture.py:15-26` |\n| API: GET file | Complete (text/plain for .mmd, application/xml for .drawio) | `architecture.py:29-48` — `get_arch_file()` |\n| API: PUT file | **Does not exist** | Needed for markdown save |\n| Path traversal protection | Complete | `progress_service.py:78-97` — `read_arch_file()` |\n| Pan/zoom per diagram | Complete | `architecture.html:1323-1375` |\n| Settings file | Located at `~/.vista/settings.json`, managed by `config.py` | `config.py:23-35` — `_resolve_settings_file()` |\n| `plantuml_server_url` | **Does not exist** anywhere | Not in `config.py` or any settings |\n| CDN: mermaid.js | Loaded | `architecture.html:6` |\n| CDN: marked.js | Loaded (for chat markdown) | `architecture.html:7` |\n| Test suite | 29 tests in `test_architecture.py`, 24 in `test_diagram_watcher.py` | All passing (139 total) |\n\n### What Needs to Change\n\n1. **arch-schema.json** (line 29) — Extend `type` enum from 2 to 6 values\n2. **diagram_watcher.py** (lines 26, 124) — Extend `WATCH_EXTENSIONS` and `_detect_diagram_type()` for new formats\n3. **progress_service.py** — Add `write_arch_file()` method (after `read_arch_file()` at line 97)\n4. **architecture.py** — Add `PUT` endpoint, update content-type mapping (lines 40-46)\n5. **architecture.html** — Refactor renderer dispatch (lines 1288-1311), add 4 new renderers + markdown edit mode\n6. **config.py** — Add `plantuml_server_url` to settings defaults (NOT a separate settings_service.py)\n7. **Tests** — Cover all new renderers, PUT endpoint, security\n\n---\n\n## Phase 1: Schema & Backend Foundation\n\n**Priority:** HIGH — All other phases depend on this\n**Estimated Complexity:** Low\n**Files:** 5 modified, 0 created\n\n### 1.1 Extend arch-schema.json Type Enum\n\n**File:** `vista/templates/arch-schema.json`\n**Line:** 29\n\nChange:\n```json\n\"enum\": [\"mermaid\", \"drawio\"]\n```\nTo:\n```json\n\"enum\": [\"mermaid\", \"drawio\", \"plantuml\", \"d2\", \"graphviz\", \"markdown\"]\n```\n\nNo other schema changes needed — `diagramType` enum already has `\"custom\"` as a catch-all for non-Mermaid diagrams. The `category` field is already optional with `architecture` and `tdd` values.\n\n### 1.2 Add write_arch_file() to ProgressService\n\n**File:** `vista/server/services/progress_service.py`\n**Insert after:** `read_arch_file()` method (line 97)\n\n```python\n@staticmethod\ndef write_arch_file(project_path: str, feature_name: str, filename: str, content: str) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Write content to a diagram file in arch/ with path traversal prevention.\n\n    Only allows writing to files with extensions: .md\n    Returns True on success, False on validation failure.\n    \"\"\"\n    WRITABLE_EXTENSIONS = {\".md\"}\n\n    safe_name = Path(filename).name\n    if safe_name != filename or \"..\" in filename:\n        return False\n\n    if Path(safe_name).suffix not in WRITABLE_EXTENSIONS:\n        return False\n\n    arch_dir = Path(project_path) / \".vista\" / \"features\" / feature_name / \"arch\"\n    target = arch_dir / safe_name\n\n    try:\n        target.resolve().relative_to(arch_dir.resolve())\n    except ValueError:\n        return False\n\n    if not arch_dir.exists():\n        return False\n\n    target.write_text(content, encoding=\"utf-8\")\n    return True\n```\n\n**Key decisions:**\n- **Writable extensions restricted to `.md` only** — Diagram files (.mmd, .puml, .d2, .dot, .drawio) are NOT writable through this API. Only markdown documentation files are editable inline.\n- **Same path traversal protection pattern** as existing `read_arch_file()` (lines 80-92).\n- **File must be in an existing arch/ directory** — won't create directories.\n\n### 1.3 Add PUT Endpoint for File Writing\n\n**File:** `vista/server/routes/architecture.py`\n**Insert after:** `get_arch_file()` function (line 48)\n\n```python\nfrom pydantic import BaseModel\n\nclass FileContent(BaseModel):\n    content: str\n\n@router.put(\"/api/projects/{project_id}/features/{feature_name}/arch/{filename}\")\nasync def put_arch_file(project_id: str, feature_name: str, filename: str, body: FileContent):\n    \"\"\"Write content to a markdown file in arch/.\"\"\"\n    project = ProjectService.get_by_id(project_id)\n    if not project:\n        raise HTTPException(status_code=404, detail=\"Project not found\")\n\n    success = ProgressService.write_arch_file(project.path, feature_name, filename, body.content)\n    if not success:\n        raise HTTPException(status_code=400, detail=\"Cannot write to this file\")\n\n    return {\"status\": \"ok\", \"filename\": filename}\n```\n\n**Note:** The `pydantic` import may already exist (check top of file). The `BaseModel` import should be added alongside existing imports if not present.\n\n### 1.4 Update Content-Type Mapping in GET Endpoint\n\n**File:** `vista/server/routes/architecture.py` — `get_arch_file()` function\n**Lines:** 40-46\n\nReplace the current if/elif content-type logic:\n```python\nif filename.endswith(\".mmd\"):\n    media_type = \"text/plain\"\nelif filename.endswith(\".drawio\"):\n    media_type = \"application/xml\"\nelse:\n    media_type = \"text/plain\"\n```\n\nWith a dictionary-based lookup:\n```python\next = filename.rsplit(\".\", 1)[-1] if \".\" in filename else \"\"\nCONTENT_TYPES = {\n    \"mmd\": \"text/plain\",\n    \"drawio\": \"application/xml\",\n    \"puml\": \"text/plain\",\n    \"d2\": \"text/plain\",\n    \"dot\": \"text/plain\",\n    \"md\": \"text/markdown\",\n}\nmedia_type = CONTENT_TYPES.get(ext, \"text/plain\")\n```\n\n### 1.5 Add PlantUML Server URL to Settings\n\n**File:** `vista/server/config.py`\n\nThe settings system uses `config.py` with defaults dicts and a `load_settings()` / `save_*()` pattern. Add a new section for diagram settings:\n\n```python\n_DIAGRAM_DEFAULTS = {\n    \"plantuml_server_url\": \"https://www.plantuml.com/plantuml\",\n}\n\ndef get_diagram_settings() -> dict:\n    \"\"\"Return merged diagram settings with defaults applied.\"\"\"\n    raw = load_settings().get(\"diagrams\", {})\n    if not isinstance(raw, dict):\n        raw = {}\n    return _merge_dicts(_DIAGRAM_DEFAULTS, raw)\n```\n\n**Also add:** A helper function or use `get_diagram_settings()` in the architecture page route to pass the PlantUML URL to the template.\n\n**Settings file effect:** When `~/.vista/settings.json` contains no `diagrams` section, the default URL (`https://www.plantuml.com/plantuml`) is used. Users can override by adding:\n```json\n{\n  \"diagrams\": {\n    \"plantuml_server_url\": \"http://localhost:8080/plantuml\"\n  }\n}\n```\n\n### 1.6 Extend Diagram Watcher Extensions\n\n**File:** `vista/server/services/diagram_watcher.py`\n\n**Change 1:** Update `WATCH_EXTENSIONS` in BOTH locations (lines 26 and 124):\n```python\nWATCH_EXTENSIONS = {\".mmd\", \".drawio\", \".puml\", \".d2\", \".dot\", \".md\"}\n```\n\n**Change 2:** Add file-type detection by extension (new function):\n```python\nEXT_TO_TYPE = {\n    \".mmd\": \"mermaid\",\n    \".drawio\": \"drawio\",\n    \".puml\": \"plantuml\",\n    \".d2\": \"d2\",\n    \".dot\": \"graphviz\",\n    \".md\": \"markdown\",\n}\n\ndef _detect_file_type(path: Path) -> str:\n    \"\"\"Detect diagram type from file extension.\"\"\"\n    return EXT_TO_TYPE.get(path.suffix.lower(), \"mermaid\")\n```\n\n**Change 3:** Update `_update_manifest_sync()` (lines 232-256) to use `_detect_file_type()` for the `type` field. For non-mermaid formats, set `diagramType: \"custom\"`. For mermaid files, continue using `_detect_diagram_type()` for the subtype.\n\n```python\n# In _update_manifest_sync():\nfor f in sorted(arch_dir.iterdir()):\n    if f.suffix in EXT_TO_TYPE and not f.name.startswith(\"_\"):\n        file_type = _detect_file_type(f)\n        diagram_type = _detect_diagram_type(f) if file_type == \"mermaid\" else \"custom\"\n        entry = {\n            \"name\": f.stem.replace(\"-\", \" \").replace(\"_\", \" \").title(),\n            \"file\": f.name,\n            \"type\": file_type,\n            \"diagramType\": diagram_type,\n            \"description\": f\"Auto-detected {file_type} diagram\",\n        }\n        diagrams.append(entry)\n```\n\n### Acceptance Criteria (Phase 1)\n\n- [ ] `arch-schema.json` validates manifests with all 6 type values\n- [ ] `PUT /api/.../arch/{filename}` writes `.md` files successfully\n- [ ] `PUT /api/.../arch/{filename}` returns 400 for non-`.md` files\n- [ ] `PUT /api/.../arch/{filename}` blocks path traversal attempts\n- [ ] `GET /api/.../arch/{filename}` returns correct Content-Type for all 6 extensions\n- [ ] Diagram watcher detects changes in all 6 file types\n- [ ] Manifest auto-update correctly identifies file types by extension\n- [ ] `plantuml_server_url` available via `config.get_diagram_settings()`\n\n---\n\n## Phase 2: Client-Side Renderer Infrastructure\n\n**Priority:** HIGH — Core rendering dispatch\n**Depends on:** Phase 1\n**Estimated Complexity:** Medium\n**Files:** 1 modified (architecture.html), CDN scripts added\n\n### 2.1 Refactor Renderer Dispatch\n\n**File:** `vista/server/views/architecture.html`\n**Replace:** `renderDiagramContent()` function (lines 1288-1311)\n\nCurrently checks `filename.endsWith('.mmd')` and falls back to `<pre>`. Refactor to a renderer map:\n\n```javascript\nconst RENDERERS = {\n    mermaid:  renderMermaid,\n    plantuml: renderPlantUML,\n    d2:       renderD2,\n    graphviz: renderGraphviz,\n    drawio:   renderDrawio,\n    markdown: renderMarkdown,\n};\n\nasync function renderDiagramContent(el, filename, content, idx, diagramType) {\n    // diagramType is the 'type' field from manifest (mermaid, plantuml, etc.)\n    const renderer = RENDERERS[diagramType];\n    if (renderer) {\n        return renderer(el, content, idx, filename);\n    }\n    // Unknown type fallback\n    el.innerHTML = `<pre class=\"text-gray-400 text-xs whitespace-pre-wrap\">${escapeHtml(content)}</pre>`;\n}\n```\n\n**Critical change:** `loadDiagrams()` must pass the manifest `type` field to `renderDiagramContent()`. Currently only passes filename/content/idx. Add `diagram.type` as 5th parameter.\n\n### 2.2 Mermaid Renderer (Extract from existing)\n\nExtract the existing mermaid logic (lines 1289-1307) into a standalone function:\n\n```javascript\nasync function renderMermaid(el, content, idx, filename) {\n    try {\n        const id = `mermaid-svg-${idx}-${++mermaidCounter}`;\n        const { svg } = await mermaid.render(id, content);\n        el.innerHTML = svg;\n        // Existing node click handlers...\n        el.querySelectorAll('.node').forEach(node => {\n            node.style.cursor = 'pointer';\n            node.addEventListener('click', (e) => {\n                e.stopPropagation();\n                toggleNodeSelection(node, idx);\n            });\n        });\n        reapplySelections(idx);\n    } catch (e) {\n        el.innerHTML = `<pre class=\"text-yellow-400 text-xs whitespace-pre-wrap\">Mermaid parse error:\\n${e.message || e}\\n\\n${content}</pre>`;\n    }\n}\n```\n\n### 2.3 PlantUML Renderer\n\n**CDN dependency:** `plantuml-encoder` v1.4.0 (~10KB minified)\n```html\n<script src=\"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/plantuml-encoder@1.4.0/dist/plantuml-encoder.min.js\"></script>\n```\n\n**Template variable needed:** Pass `PLANTUML_SERVER_URL` from server context.\n\n**Implementation:**\n```javascript\nasync function renderPlantUML(el, content, idx, filename) {\n    try {\n        const encoded = plantumlEncoder.encode(content);\n        const svgUrl = `${PLANTUML_SERVER_URL}/svg/${encoded}`;\n        const resp = await fetch(svgUrl);\n        if (!resp.ok) throw new Error(`PlantUML server error: ${resp.status}`);\n        const svg = await resp.text();\n        el.innerHTML = svg;\n    } catch (err) {\n        el.innerHTML = `<div class=\"diagram-error\">\n            <p class=\"text-yellow-400 text-sm mb-2\">PlantUML render error: ${escapeHtml(err.message)}</p>\n            <pre class=\"text-gray-400 text-xs whitespace-pre-wrap\">${escapeHtml(content)}</pre>\n        </div>`;\n    }\n}\n```\n\n**Error handling:**\n- Server unreachable → Show error message + raw source as fallback\n- Invalid syntax → PlantUML server returns an error image; show the raw source too\n\n### 2.4 D2 Renderer\n\n**Dependency status:** `@terrastruct/d2` does NOT have a well-known browser-compatible WASM build available on CDN. After research:\n\n- **d2 official repo** (`terrastruct/d2`) is a Go binary, no WASM distribution\n- **No `@anthropic-ai/d2-wasm`** package exists on npm\n- **Kroki** is a self-hosted diagram server that supports D2 (like PlantUML server)\n\n**Revised approach — Server-side rendering via Kroki or raw source fallback:**\n\n```javascript\nasync function renderD2(el, content, idx, filename) {\n    // Attempt 1: If a Kroki server is configured, render via server\n    if (window.KROKI_SERVER_URL) {\n        try {\n            const resp = await fetch(`${KROKI_SERVER_URL}/d2/svg`, {\n                method: 'POST',\n                headers: { 'Content-Type': 'text/plain' },\n                body: content,\n            });\n            if (resp.ok) {\n                el.innerHTML = await resp.text();\n                return;\n            }\n        } catch (_) { /* fall through */ }\n    }\n    // Fallback: Syntax-highlighted raw source\n    el.innerHTML = `<div class=\"diagram-raw-source\">\n        <p class=\"text-blue-400 text-sm mb-2\">D2 diagram (raw source — install Kroki for live rendering)</p>\n        <pre class=\"text-gray-300 text-xs whitespace-pre-wrap\">${escapeHtml(content)}</pre>\n    </div>`;\n}\n```\n\n**Decision:** D2 rendering ships as raw-source-with-syntax-hint initially. Kroki integration (optional) is documented but not required. This avoids a hard dependency on a non-existent WASM package.\n\n**Future enhancement:** If `@anthropic-ai/d2-wasm` or similar becomes available, swap in client-side rendering.\n\n### 2.5 Graphviz Renderer\n\n**CDN dependency:** `@viz-js/viz` v3 — well-established WASM package (~2.5MB)\n\nThe package provides a standalone build that works in browsers. Load lazily:\n\n```javascript\nlet vizInstance = null;\n\nasync function loadViz() {\n    if (vizInstance) return vizInstance;\n    // Dynamic script load\n    if (!window.Viz) {\n        await new Promise((resolve, reject) => {\n            const script = document.createElement('script');\n            script.src = 'https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/@viz-js/viz@3.11.0/lib/viz-standalone.js';\n            script.onload = resolve;\n            script.onerror = reject;\n            document.head.appendChild(script);\n        });\n    }\n    vizInstance = await Viz.instance();\n    return vizInstance;\n}\n\nasync function renderGraphviz(el, content, idx, filename) {\n    try {\n        const viz = await loadViz();\n        const svg = viz.renderSVGElement(content);\n        el.innerHTML = '';\n        el.appendChild(svg);\n    } catch (err) {\n        el.innerHTML = `<div class=\"diagram-error\">\n            <p class=\"text-yellow-400 text-sm mb-2\">Graphviz render error: ${escapeHtml(err.message)}</p>\n            <pre class=\"text-gray-400 text-xs whitespace-pre-wrap\">${escapeHtml(content)}</pre>\n        </div>`;\n    }\n}\n```\n\n**Engine selection:** Default to `dot` layout engine. Graphviz supports `dot`, `neato`, `fdp`, `sfdp`, `circo`, `twopi`, `osage`, `patchwork`. Could expose engine via manifest `layoutEngine` field in future — not in scope now.\n\n### 2.6 Draw.io Renderer\n\n**Current state:** Falls through to `<pre>` tag with escaped XML content. No rendering.\n\n**Implementation using Draw.io viewer iframe:**\n```javascript\nfunction renderDrawio(el, content, idx, filename) {\n    try {\n        // Use postMessage API for large files (URL encoding may exceed limits)\n        const iframe = document.createElement('iframe');\n        iframe.style.width = '100%';\n        iframe.style.height = '500px';\n        iframe.style.border = 'none';\n        iframe.style.borderRadius = '8px';\n        iframe.setAttribute('sandbox', 'allow-scripts allow-same-origin');\n\n        // Base64 encode to avoid URL length limits\n        const b64 = btoa(unescape(encodeURIComponent(content)));\n        iframe.src = `https://viewer.diagrams.net/?highlight=0000ff&nav=1&title=${encodeURIComponent(filename)}#R${b64}`;\n\n        el.innerHTML = '';\n        el.appendChild(iframe);\n    } catch (err) {\n        el.innerHTML = `<div class=\"diagram-error\">\n            <p class=\"text-yellow-400 text-sm mb-2\">Draw.io render error: ${escapeHtml(err.message)}</p>\n            <pre class=\"text-gray-400 text-xs whitespace-pre-wrap\">${escapeHtml(content)}</pre>\n        </div>`;\n    }\n}\n```\n\n**Risk:** Very large `.drawio` files may exceed URL limits even with base64 encoding. For MVP, this approach is acceptable. For large files, the `postMessage` API approach can be added later.\n\n### 2.7 Markdown Renderer\n\n**Library:** `marked.js` — **already loaded** in `architecture.html` (line 7). No additional CDN script needed.\n\n```javascript\nfunction renderMarkdown(el, content, idx, filename) {\n    try {\n        const html = marked.parse(content);\n        el.innerHTML = `<div class=\"markdown-content\">${html}</div>`;\n        // Store original content for edit mode\n        el.dataset.rawContent = content;\n        el.dataset.filename = filename;\n        el.dataset.idx = idx;\n    } catch (err) {\n        el.innerHTML = `<pre class=\"text-gray-400 text-xs whitespace-pre-wrap\">${escapeHtml(content)}</pre>`;\n    }\n}\n```\n\n### Acceptance Criteria (Phase 2)\n\n- [ ] Mermaid diagrams continue to render correctly (no regression)\n- [ ] PlantUML diagrams render as SVG via server fetch\n- [ ] D2 diagrams show raw source with info message (or Kroki SVG if configured)\n- [ ] Graphviz diagrams render via `@viz-js/viz` WASM\n- [ ] Draw.io diagrams render in iframe (not raw XML)\n- [ ] Markdown files render as formatted HTML via `marked.js`\n- [ ] Each renderer shows error + raw source on failure\n- [ ] WASM module (Graphviz) loads lazily\n- [ ] PlantUML encoder loads eagerly (small, ~10KB)\n\n---\n\n## Phase 3: Markdown Inline Editor\n\n**Priority:** HIGH — Key new user interaction\n**Depends on:** Phase 1 (PUT endpoint), Phase 2 (markdown renderer)\n**Estimated Complexity:** Medium-High\n**Files:** 1 modified (architecture.html), 1 modified (arch-chat.css or inline styles)\n\n### 3.1 Edit Button on Markdown Cards\n\nWhen building diagram cards in JavaScript (NOT Jinja2 — cards are built client-side), check the diagram type from the manifest entry:\n\n```javascript\nfunction buildDiagramCard(diagram, idx) {\n    // ... existing card structure ...\n    const editButton = diagram.type === 'markdown'\n        ? `<button class=\"md-edit-btn\" onclick=\"toggleMarkdownEdit(${idx})\" title=\"Edit markdown\">✎</button>`\n        : '';\n    // Insert into card header alongside existing zoom controls\n}\n```\n\n**Placement:** In the diagram card header template area of `architecture.html` — identify where card headers are constructed (likely near line 1016-1041) and add the edit button conditionally.\n\n### 3.2 Edit Mode State Machine\n\n**States:** `view` → `editing` → `saving` → `view`\n\n```javascript\nconst markdownEditState = {};  // idx -> { editing: bool, saving: bool, originalContent: string }\n\nfunction toggleMarkdownEdit(idx) {\n    const state = markdownEditState[idx] || { editing: false };\n    if (state.editing) {\n        cancelMarkdownEdit(idx);\n    } else {\n        enterMarkdownEdit(idx);\n    }\n}\n\nfunction enterMarkdownEdit(idx) {\n    const el = document.getElementById(`diagram-viewport-${idx}`);\n    const content = el.dataset.rawContent || diagramContents[DIAGRAMS[idx].file];\n\n    markdownEditState[idx] = { editing: true, saving: false, originalContent: content };\n\n    el.innerHTML = `\n        <div class=\"md-editor-container\">\n            <div class=\"md-editor-toolbar\">\n                <button class=\"md-save-btn\" onclick=\"saveMarkdown(${idx})\" title=\"Save\">✓ Save</button>\n                <button class=\"md-cancel-btn\" onclick=\"cancelMarkdownEdit(${idx})\" title=\"Cancel\">✕ Cancel</button>\n                <span class=\"md-save-indicator\" id=\"md-indicator-${idx}\"></span>\n            </div>\n            <textarea class=\"md-editor\" id=\"md-textarea-${idx}\" spellcheck=\"false\">${escapeHtml(content)}</textarea>\n        </div>\n    `;\n\n    const textarea = document.getElementById(`md-textarea-${idx}`);\n    textarea.focus();\n    autoResizeTextarea(textarea);\n    textarea.addEventListener('input', () => autoResizeTextarea(textarea));\n\n    updateEditButton(idx, true);\n}\n\nfunction cancelMarkdownEdit(idx) {\n    const state = markdownEditState[idx];\n    if (!state) return;\n\n    const el = document.getElementById(`diagram-viewport-${idx}`);\n    renderMarkdown(el, state.originalContent, idx, DIAGRAMS[idx].file);\n\n    markdownEditState[idx] = { editing: false };\n    updateEditButton(idx, false);\n}\n\nasync function saveMarkdown(idx) {\n    const state = markdownEditState[idx];\n    if (!state || state.saving) return;\n\n    const textarea = document.getElementById(`md-textarea-${idx}`);\n    const newContent = textarea.value;\n    const filename = DIAGRAMS[idx].file;\n    const indicator = document.getElementById(`md-indicator-${idx}`);\n\n    state.saving = true;\n    indicator.textContent = 'Saving...';\n    indicator.className = 'md-save-indicator saving';\n\n    try {\n        const resp = await fetch(\n            `/api/projects/${PROJECT_ID}/features/${FEATURE_NAME}/arch/${filename}`,\n            {\n                method: 'PUT',\n                headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },\n                body: JSON.stringify({ content: newContent }),\n            }\n        );\n\n        if (!resp.ok) throw new Error(`Save failed: ${resp.status}`);\n\n        indicator.textContent = 'Saved!';\n        indicator.className = 'md-save-indicator saved';\n\n        // Update stored content\n        diagramContents[filename] = newContent;\n\n        // Return to view mode after brief success indicator\n        setTimeout(() => {\n            const el = document.getElementById(`diagram-viewport-${idx}`);\n            renderMarkdown(el, newContent, idx, filename);\n            markdownEditState[idx] = { editing: false };\n            updateEditButton(idx, false);\n        }, 800);\n\n    } catch (err) {\n        indicator.textContent = `Error: ${err.message}`;\n        indicator.className = 'md-save-indicator error';\n        state.saving = false;\n    }\n}\n\nfunction autoResizeTextarea(textarea) {\n    textarea.style.height = 'auto';\n    textarea.style.height = Math.max(200, textarea.scrollHeight) + 'px';\n}\n\nfunction updateEditButton(idx, isEditing) {\n    const btn = document.querySelector(`[data-edit-idx=\"${idx}\"]`);\n    if (btn) {\n        btn.textContent = isEditing ? '✕' : '✎';\n        btn.title = isEditing ? 'Cancel editing' : 'Edit markdown';\n    }\n}\n```\n\n### 3.3 Keyboard Shortcuts\n\n```javascript\ndocument.addEventListener('keydown', (e) => {\n    for (const [idx, state] of Object.entries(markdownEditState)) {\n        if (state.editing) {\n            if ((e.ctrlKey || e.metaKey) && e.key === 's') {\n                e.preventDefault();\n                saveMarkdown(parseInt(idx));\n            } else if (e.key === 'Escape') {\n                e.preventDefault();\n                cancelMarkdownEdit(parseInt(idx));\n            }\n        }\n    }\n});\n```\n\n### 3.4 Editor CSS Styles\n\n**File:** `vista/server/views/static/arch-chat.css` (or inline in architecture.html `<style>` block)\n\n```css\n.md-editor-container {\n    display: flex;\n    flex-direction: column;\n    height: 100%;\n    min-height: 200px;\n}\n\n.md-editor-toolbar {\n    display: flex;\n    align-items: center;\n    gap: 8px;\n    padding: 8px 12px;\n    background: var(--surface-2, #1e293b);\n    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border, #334155);\n}\n\n.md-editor {\n    flex: 1;\n    resize: vertical;\n    min-height: 200px;\n    padding: 16px;\n    font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', 'Fira Code', monospace;\n    font-size: 14px;\n    line-height: 1.6;\n    background: var(--surface-1, #0f172a);\n    color: var(--text-primary, #e2e8f0);\n    border: none;\n    outline: none;\n}\n\n.md-edit-btn {\n    cursor: pointer;\n    padding: 4px 8px;\n    border-radius: 4px;\n    opacity: 0.6;\n    transition: opacity 0.2s;\n}\n.md-edit-btn:hover { opacity: 1; }\n\n.md-save-btn { color: #4ade80; cursor: pointer; }\n.md-cancel-btn { color: #f87171; cursor: pointer; }\n.md-save-indicator.saving { color: #facc15; }\n.md-save-indicator.saved { color: #4ade80; }\n.md-save-indicator.error { color: #f87171; }\n\n.markdown-content {\n    padding: 16px;\n    line-height: 1.7;\n}\n.markdown-content h1, .markdown-content h2, .markdown-content h3 {\n    margin-top: 1.5em;\n    margin-bottom: 0.5em;\n}\n.markdown-content pre {\n    background: var(--surface-2, #1e293b);\n    padding: 12px;\n    border-radius: 6px;\n    overflow-x: auto;\n}\n.markdown-content code {\n    background: var(--surface-2, #1e293b);\n    padding: 2px 6px;\n    border-radius: 3px;\n    font-size: 0.9em;\n}\n.markdown-content table {\n    border-collapse: collapse;\n    width: 100%;\n}\n.markdown-content th, .markdown-content td {\n    border: 1px solid var(--border, #334155);\n    padding: 8px 12px;\n    text-align: left;\n}\n```\n\n### Acceptance Criteria (Phase 3)\n\n- [ ] Markdown files render as formatted HTML with GFM support (tables, code blocks, task lists)\n- [ ] Edit button appears only on markdown-type diagram cards\n- [ ] Clicking edit switches to textarea with raw content\n- [ ] Save writes content to disk via PUT API and returns to rendered view\n- [ ] Cancel discards changes and returns to rendered view\n- [ ] Save indicator shows progress (saving → saved → hidden)\n- [ ] Save failure shows error message, does not lose edits\n- [ ] Ctrl+S / Cmd+S saves, Escape cancels\n- [ ] Content stored in `diagramContents` is updated after successful save\n\n---\n\n## Phase 4: Template & Watcher Integration\n\n**Priority:** MEDIUM\n**Depends on:** Phases 1-3\n**Estimated Complexity:** Low-Medium\n**Files:** 2 modified (architecture.html, architecture.py route)\n\n### 4.1 Pass Manifest Type to Renderers\n\n**File:** `vista/server/views/architecture.html`\n\nUpdate `loadDiagrams()` to pass the manifest `type` field:\n\n```javascript\nasync function loadDiagrams() {\n    for (let i = 0; i < DIAGRAMS.length; i++) {\n        const diagram = DIAGRAMS[i];\n        const resp = await fetch(`/api/projects/${PROJECT_ID}/features/${FEATURE_NAME}/arch/${diagram.file}`);\n        const content = await resp.text();\n        diagramContents[diagram.file] = content;\n\n        const el = document.getElementById(`diagram-viewport-${i}`);\n        renderDiagramContent(el, diagram.file, content, i, diagram.type);  // 5th arg: type\n    }\n}\n```\n\n### 4.2 Conditionally Show Edit Button in Card Header\n\nWhen building diagram cards (JavaScript), check the diagram type:\n\n```javascript\n// Inside card header construction\nconst editButton = diagram.type === 'markdown'\n    ? `<button class=\"md-edit-btn\" data-edit-idx=\"${idx}\" onclick=\"toggleMarkdownEdit(${idx})\" title=\"Edit\">✎</button>`\n    : '';\n```\n\n### 4.3 CDN Script Loading\n\n**File:** `vista/server/views/architecture.html` — `<head>` section\n\nAdd after existing mermaid.js and marked.js CDN lines:\n\n```html\n<!-- PlantUML encoder (small, ~10KB) — loaded eagerly -->\n<script src=\"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/plantuml-encoder@1.4.0/dist/plantuml-encoder.min.js\"></script>\n\n<!-- @viz-js/viz loaded lazily by renderGraphviz() — no eager script needed -->\n<!-- Draw.io viewer loaded as iframe — no script needed -->\n```\n\n### 4.4 PlantUML Server URL Injection\n\n**File:** `vista/server/routes/architecture.py` — `architecture_viewer_page()` (line 51-66)\n\nAdd the PlantUML server URL to the template context:\n\n```python\nfrom server.config import get_diagram_settings\n\n@router.get(\"/project/{project_id}/arch/{feature_name}\", response_class=HTMLResponse)\nasync def architecture_viewer_page(request: Request, project_id: str, feature_name: str):\n    # ... existing code ...\n    diagram_settings = get_diagram_settings()\n    plantuml_url = diagram_settings.get(\"plantuml_server_url\", \"https://www.plantuml.com/plantuml\")\n    return templates.TemplateResponse(\"architecture.html\", {\n        \"request\": request,\n        # ... existing context vars ...\n        \"plantuml_url\": plantuml_url,\n    })\n```\n\nAnd in the template:\n```html\n<script>\n    const PLANTUML_SERVER_URL = {{ plantuml_url | tojson }};\n</script>\n```\n\n### Acceptance Criteria (Phase 4)\n\n- [ ] All 6 diagram types dispatch to their correct renderer via `diagram.type`\n- [ ] Edit button only appears on markdown cards\n- [ ] PlantUML server URL passed from settings to frontend\n- [ ] PlantUML encoder CDN script loaded\n- [ ] Graphviz WASM loads lazily on first Graphviz diagram\n\n---\n\n## Phase 5: Tests\n\n**Priority:** HIGH — Must validate security and correctness\n**Depends on:** Phases 1-4\n**Estimated Complexity:** Medium\n**Files:** 2 modified (test_architecture.py, test_diagram_watcher.py)\n\n### 5.1 PUT Endpoint Tests\n\n**File:** `vista/tests/test_architecture.py`\n**Add class:** `TestArchWriteAPI` (after existing `TestArchitectureAPI` at line 227)\n\n```python\nclass TestArchWriteAPI:\n    def test_put_markdown_file_success(self, api_env):\n        \"\"\"PUT .md file writes content and returns 200.\"\"\"\n\n    def test_put_non_markdown_file_rejected(self, api_env):\n        \"\"\"PUT .mmd file returns 400.\"\"\"\n\n    def test_put_path_traversal_blocked(self, api_env):\n        \"\"\"PUT ../../evil.md returns 400.\"\"\"\n\n    def test_put_dotdot_in_filename(self, api_env):\n        \"\"\"PUT with '..' anywhere in filename returns 400.\"\"\"\n\n    def test_put_project_not_found(self, api_env):\n        \"\"\"PUT to nonexistent project returns 404.\"\"\"\n\n    def test_put_no_arch_directory(self, api_env):\n        \"\"\"PUT to feature without arch/ returns 400.\"\"\"\n\n    def test_put_verify_file_written(self, api_env):\n        \"\"\"After successful PUT, GET returns the new content.\"\"\"\n```\n\n### 5.2 ProgressService Write Tests\n\n**File:** `vista/tests/test_architecture.py`\n**Add class:** `TestProgressServiceWrite` (after existing `TestProgressServiceArch` at line 318)\n\n```python\nclass TestProgressServiceWrite:\n    def test_write_arch_file_md_success(self, tmp_path):\n        \"\"\"write_arch_file() writes .md content to arch/.\"\"\"\n\n    def test_write_arch_file_mmd_rejected(self, tmp_path):\n        \"\"\"write_arch_file() rejects .mmd files.\"\"\"\n\n    def test_write_arch_file_puml_rejected(self, tmp_path):\n        \"\"\"write_arch_file() rejects .puml files.\"\"\"\n\n    def test_write_arch_file_path_traversal(self, tmp_path):\n        \"\"\"write_arch_file() blocks ../evil path.\"\"\"\n\n    def test_write_arch_file_no_arch_dir(self, tmp_path):\n        \"\"\"write_arch_file() returns False when arch/ doesn't exist.\"\"\"\n\n    def test_write_arch_file_overwrites_existing(self, tmp_path):\n        \"\"\"write_arch_file() overwrites an existing .md file.\"\"\"\n```\n\n### 5.3 Extended Schema Validation Tests\n\n**File:** `vista/tests/test_architecture.py`\n**Add to existing `TestSchemaValidation` class** (line 320)\n\n```python\ndef test_arch_schema_accepts_plantuml_type(self):\ndef test_arch_schema_accepts_d2_type(self):\ndef test_arch_schema_accepts_graphviz_type(self):\ndef test_arch_schema_accepts_markdown_type(self):\n# Note: test_arch_schema_rejects_invalid_type already exists (line 416)\n```\n\n### 5.4 Content-Type Tests\n\n**File:** `vista/tests/test_architecture.py`\n**Add class:** `TestContentTypes`\n\n```python\nclass TestContentTypes:\n    def test_get_puml_returns_text_plain(self, api_env):\n    def test_get_d2_returns_text_plain(self, api_env):\n    def test_get_dot_returns_text_plain(self, api_env):\n    def test_get_md_returns_text_markdown(self, api_env):\n```\n\n### 5.5 Diagram Watcher Extension Tests\n\n**File:** `vista/tests/test_diagram_watcher.py`\n**Add class:** `TestExtendedFileTypes` (after existing `TestManifestUpdate` at line 193)\n\n```python\nclass TestExtendedFileTypes:\n    def test_watches_puml_files(self):\n        \"\"\"WATCH_EXTENSIONS includes .puml.\"\"\"\n\n    def test_watches_d2_files(self):\n        \"\"\"WATCH_EXTENSIONS includes .d2.\"\"\"\n\n    def test_watches_dot_files(self):\n        \"\"\"WATCH_EXTENSIONS includes .dot.\"\"\"\n\n    def test_watches_md_files(self):\n        \"\"\"WATCH_EXTENSIONS includes .md.\"\"\"\n\n    def test_detect_file_type_plantuml(self):\n        \"\"\"_detect_file_type() returns 'plantuml' for .puml.\"\"\"\n\n    def test_detect_file_type_d2(self):\n        \"\"\"_detect_file_type() returns 'd2' for .d2.\"\"\"\n\n    def test_detect_file_type_graphviz(self):\n        \"\"\"_detect_file_type() returns 'graphviz' for .dot.\"\"\"\n\n    def test_detect_file_type_markdown(self):\n        \"\"\"_detect_file_type() returns 'markdown' for .md.\"\"\"\n\n    def test_manifest_update_assigns_correct_type_plantuml(self):\n        \"\"\"Manifest update sets type='plantuml' for .puml files.\"\"\"\n\n    def test_manifest_update_assigns_correct_type_markdown(self):\n        \"\"\"Manifest update sets type='markdown' for .md files.\"\"\"\n```\n\n### 5.6 Settings Tests\n\n**File:** `vista/tests/test_architecture.py` (or new `test_config.py` if appropriate)\n\n```python\nclass TestDiagramSettings:\n    def test_get_diagram_settings_default(self):\n        \"\"\"Default plantuml_server_url is plantuml.com.\"\"\"\n\n    def test_get_diagram_settings_override(self):\n        \"\"\"Custom plantuml_server_url from settings.json is returned.\"\"\"\n```\n\n### Test Count Summary\n\n| Category | New Tests | Location |\n|----------|-----------|----------|\n| PUT endpoint | 7 | `test_architecture.py` |\n| ProgressService write | 6 | `test_architecture.py` |\n| Schema validation | 4 | `test_architecture.py` |\n| Content types | 4 | `test_architecture.py` |\n| Diagram watcher extensions | 10 | `test_diagram_watcher.py` |\n| Settings | 2 | `test_architecture.py` |\n| **Total new** | **33** | |\n\n### Acceptance Criteria (Phase 5)\n\n- [ ] All PUT endpoint tests pass (including security: path traversal, extension whitelist)\n- [ ] All schema validation tests pass for 6 types\n- [ ] Content-type tests pass for all new extensions\n- [ ] Watcher tests pass for all 6 file types\n- [ ] Settings tests pass for defaults and overrides\n- [ ] No regressions in existing 53 tests (29 arch + 24 watcher)\n- [ ] Total test count: ~86 (53 existing + 33 new)\n\n---\n\n## Phase 6: Documentation & Skill Updates\n\n**Priority:** LOW\n**Depends on:** All prior phases\n**Estimated Complexity:** Low\n\n### 6.1 Update Plan Skill SKILL.md\n\n**File:** `vista/skills/plan/SKILL.md`\n\nUpdate Step 3 (architecture generation) to mention all supported formats:\n- Default: Mermaid (.mmd) for all diagram types\n- Optional: PlantUML (.puml) for detailed UML class/sequence diagrams\n- Optional: D2 (.d2) for architecture diagrams (raw source unless Kroki configured)\n- Optional: Graphviz (.dot) for dependency graphs\n- Optional: Markdown (.md) for prose documentation (design rationale, ADRs)\n\n### 6.2 Update Diagrams Skill\n\n**File:** `vista/skills/diagrams/SKILL.md`\n\nDocument the expanded format support.\n\n### 6.3 Update Specs\n\n**arch-directory.md:**\n- Update supported types from `\"mermaid\" | \"drawio\"` to all 6 values\n- Update data model DiagramEntry type union\n- Add markdown editing workflow\n\n**rendering-pipeline.md:**\n- Update renderer table to include all 6 renderers\n- Add CDN dependency table\n- Document lazy vs eager loading strategy\n\n### Acceptance Criteria (Phase 6)\n\n- [ ] Plan skill lists all supported formats\n- [ ] Diagrams skill documents expanded support\n- [ ] Specs updated to reflect all 6 types\n- [ ] Renderer table complete in rendering-pipeline.md\n\n---\n\n## Risk Assessment\n\n| Risk | Likelihood | Impact | Mitigation |\n|------|-----------|--------|------------|\n| D2 WASM not available as browser-compatible package | **Confirmed** | Low | Ship with raw source display + optional Kroki integration |\n| PlantUML server rate limiting or network issues | Low | Low | Self-hosted server option in settings; error + raw source fallback |\n| `@viz-js/viz` WASM too large (>5MB) | Low | Medium | Lazy load only when Graphviz diagram appears; ~2.5MB actual |\n| Draw.io viewer base64 URL exceeds limits for large files | Medium | Medium | Base64 approach for MVP; postMessage API for future |\n| Markdown editor unsaved changes lost on navigation | Low | Medium | Add `beforeunload` warning when editing (enhancement) |\n| `marked.js` XSS via user-edited markdown | Low | High | Use `marked` with default sanitization; content is user-owned files |\n\n---\n\n## Implementation Order (Recommended)\n\n1. **Phase 1** — Backend foundation (schema, PUT endpoint, watcher extensions, settings)\n2. **Phase 5 partial** — Backend tests for Phase 1 (schema, PUT, watcher, settings) — validate before frontend\n3. **Phase 2** — Renderer infrastructure (dispatch refactor + all 6 renderers)\n4. **Phase 3** — Markdown editor (edit mode, save/cancel, keyboard shortcuts)\n5. **Phase 4** — Template integration (type passing, CDN loading, URL injection)\n6. **Phase 5 remainder** — Content type tests, integration tests\n7. **Phase 6** — Documentation\n\n**Estimated total:** ~3-4 build iterations\n\n---\n\n## Files Summary\n\n### Files to Modify\n\n| File | Changes |\n|------|---------|\n| `vista/templates/arch-schema.json` | Extend `type` enum: add `plantuml`, `d2`, `graphviz`, `markdown` (line 29) |\n| `vista/server/services/progress_service.py` | Add `write_arch_file()` method (after line 97) |\n| `vista/server/routes/architecture.py` | Add PUT endpoint (after line 48), update content-type mapping (lines 40-46) |\n| `vista/server/views/architecture.html` | Refactor renderer dispatch (lines 1288-1311), add 5 new renderers, add markdown editor, CDN scripts |\n| `vista/server/views/static/arch-chat.css` | Add markdown editor + content styles |\n| `vista/server/services/diagram_watcher.py` | Extend `WATCH_EXTENSIONS` (lines 26, 124), add `_detect_file_type()`, update `_update_manifest_sync()` |\n| `vista/server/config.py` | Add `_DIAGRAM_DEFAULTS` and `get_diagram_settings()` |\n| `vista/tests/test_architecture.py` | Add ~23 new tests (PUT, schema, content types, settings) |\n| `vista/tests/test_diagram_watcher.py` | Add ~10 new tests (extended file types, type detection) |\n\n### Files to Create\n\nNone — all changes are modifications to existing files.\n\n### Settings Changes\n\n| Setting | Default Value | Location |\n|---------|--------------|----------|\n| `diagrams.plantuml_server_url` | `\"https://www.plantuml.com/plantuml\"` | `~/.vista/settings.json` via `config.py` |\n\n---\n\n## Key Corrections from Iteration 1\n\n| # | Iteration 1 Claim | Correction |