{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01YK1FaeKip8hEsErT6J4wdy","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# Spec: Architecture Directory Structure\n     2→\n     3→> Updated: 2026-02-15 — diagramType enum and category field aligned with arch-schema.json\n     4→\n     5→## Overview\n     6→\n     7→File-based architecture directory with manifest for storing native diagram files per feature.\n     8→\n     9→## Parent JTBD\n    10→\n    11→As a developer, I want diagrams stored as native files so I can edit them with standard tools and agents can generate them directly.\n    12→\n    13→## Scope\n    14→\n    15→**In Scope:**\n    16→- `arch/` subdirectory creation within `.vista/features/<name>/`\n    17→- `_arch.json` manifest schema and validation\n    18→- `_plan.json` reference to arch directory via `architecture.ref`\n    19→- Setup script updates to scaffold arch/ directory\n    20→\n    21→**Out of Scope:**\n    22→- Diagram content rendering (see rendering-pipeline spec)\n    23→- AI chat review (see chat-review spec)\n    24→- Migration of existing plans (see migration spec)\n    25→\n    26→## Requirements\n    27→\n    28→### Functional\n    29→\n    30→1. Each feature directory gets an `arch/` subdirectory when scaffolded\n    31→2. `_arch.json` manifest contains an array of diagram entries with: `name`, `file`, `type`, `diagramType`, `description`, and optional `category`\n    32→3. Supported types: `\"mermaid\"` and `\"drawio\"`\n    33→4. Supported diagramTypes: `\"flowchart\"`, `\"sequence\"`, `\"state\"`, `\"er\"`, `\"gantt\"`, `\"architecture\"`, `\"wireframe\"`, `\"custom\"`, `\"logic-flow\"`, `\"decision-tree\"`, `\"test-contract\"`\n    34→5. Supported categories: `\"architecture\"` (default), `\"tdd\"` — used for grouping and filtering diagram entries\n    35→6. `_plan.json` includes `\"architecture\": { \"ref\": \"./arch/_arch.json\" }` at the top level\n    36→7. Plan JSON no longer requires `uiFlows`, `dataModels`, `dataFlow`, `services` sections - these are replaced by arch/ files\n    37→\n    38→### Non-Functional\n    39→\n    40→- **Performance:** Manifest file < 10KB (metadata only, no content)\n    41→- **Platform:** File system (cross-platform paths)\n    42→\n    43→## User Workflows\n    44→\n    45→### Workflow 1: Agent Generates Architecture\n    46→\n    47→**Actor:** AI agent (via /vista:plan)\n    48→**Trigger:** Step 5 of plan workflow\n    49→\n    50→**Steps:**\n    51→1. Agent creates `arch/` directory\n    52→2. Agent writes .mmd files for each diagram (system-arch, user-flow, sequence, state-model, data-model)\n    53→3. Agent writes `_arch.json` manifest referencing each file\n    54→4. Agent writes `_plan.json` with `architecture.ref` pointing to manifest\n    55→5. Feature directory is complete\n    56→\n    57→**Error Cases:**\n    58→- Invalid Mermaid syntax in .mmd file: Web renderer shows parse error inline\n    59→- Missing file referenced in manifest: Web app shows \"File not found\" placeholder\n    60→\n    61→### Workflow 2: User Adds Diagram Manually\n    62→\n    63→**Actor:** Developer\n    64→**Trigger:** User wants to add a diagram outside the plan workflow\n    65→\n    66→**Steps:**\n    67→1. User creates a .mmd or .drawio file in arch/\n    68→2. User adds an entry to _arch.json manually or via CLI\n    69→3. Web app picks up the new diagram on next page load\n    70→\n    71→**Error Cases:**\n    72→- Malformed _arch.json: Server returns 400 with validation error\n    73→\n    74→## Data Model\n    75→\n    76→**Entities:**\n    77→- ArchManifest: `{ feature: string, diagrams: DiagramEntry[] }`\n    78→- DiagramEntry: `{ name: string, file: string, type: \"mermaid\"|\"drawio\", diagramType: string, category?: \"architecture\"|\"tdd\", description: string }`\n    79→\n    80→**Relationships:**\n    81→- ArchManifest 1:N DiagramEntry\n    82→- Feature 1:1 ArchManifest (via _plan.json reference)\n    83→\n    84→## Integration Points\n    85→\n    86→**Dependencies:**\n    87→- setup-feature.py: Must scaffold arch/ directory and empty _arch.json\n    88→\n    89→**Provides to:**\n    90→- Rendering pipeline: Manifest tells the web app what to render and how\n    91→- Chat review: Manifest provides diagram list for context injection\n    92→\n    93→## Technical Considerations\n    94→\n    95→### Architecture\n    96→- File system layer only - no database\n    97→- JSON schema validation for _arch.json\n    98→\n    99→### Patterns\n   100→- Manifest pattern (registry of files, not container of content)\n   101→- Reference pattern (_plan.json -> _arch.json)\n   102→\n   103→### Libraries/APIs\n   104→- Python `json` for manifest read/write\n   105→- `pathlib` for cross-platform path handling\n   106→\n   107→## Acceptance Criteria\n   108→\n   109→- [x] `setup-feature.py --name X` creates `arch/` directory and empty `_arch.json`\n   110→- [x] `_arch.json` validates against defined schema\n   111→- [x] `_plan.json` includes `architecture.ref` field\n   112→- [x] Plan JSON schema no longer requires uiFlows, dataModels, dataFlow, services sections\n   113→- [x] Server API can read _arch.json and return manifest data\n   114→- [x] Server API can read individual diagram file contents by manifest entry\n   115→\n   116→## Implementation Notes\n   117→\n   118→- `arch-schema.json` has been extended beyond this spec's original definition. The `diagramType` enum now includes TDD-related types (`logic-flow`, `decision-tree`, `test-contract`) and a `category` field (`architecture` | `tdd`) for grouping.\n   119→- Path traversal protection is implemented in `ProgressService.read_arch_file()` using both filename sanitization and resolved path validation.\n   120→\n   121→## Resolved Questions\n   122→\n   123→- _arch.json supports grouping via a `category` field on each diagram entry (values: `architecture`, `tdd`).\n   124→"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d91d5e1b-c8a8-412a-adba-876f560ccc8f","uuid":"8dad2f8b-9a14-4a66-b3eb-415e150870af","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:/Users/Grove/OneDrive/Documents/PYTHON/claude_plugins/vista-expanded-visualization/.vista/features/diagram_representations/specs/arch-directory.md","content":"# Spec: Architecture Directory Structure\n\n> Updated: 2026-02-15 — diagramType enum and category field aligned with arch-schema.json\n\n## Overview\n\nFile-based architecture directory with manifest for storing native diagram files per feature.\n\n## Parent JTBD\n\nAs a developer, I want diagrams stored as native files so I can edit them with standard tools and agents can generate them directly.\n\n## Scope\n\n**In Scope:**\n- `arch/` subdirectory creation within `.vista/features/<name>/`\n- `_arch.json` manifest schema and validation\n- `_plan.json` reference to arch directory via `architecture.ref`\n- Setup script updates to scaffold arch/ directory\n\n**Out of Scope:**\n- Diagram content rendering (see rendering-pipeline spec)\n- AI chat review (see chat-review spec)\n- Migration of existing plans (see migration spec)\n\n## Requirements\n\n### Functional\n\n1. Each feature directory gets an `arch/` subdirectory when scaffolded\n2. `_arch.json` manifest contains an array of diagram entries with: `name`, `file`, `type`, `diagramType`, `description`, and optional `category`\n3. Supported types: `\"mermaid\"` and `\"drawio\"`\n4. Supported diagramTypes: `\"flowchart\"`, `\"sequence\"`, `\"state\"`, `\"er\"`, `\"gantt\"`, `\"architecture\"`, `\"wireframe\"`, `\"custom\"`, `\"logic-flow\"`, `\"decision-tree\"`, `\"test-contract\"`\n5. Supported categories: `\"architecture\"` (default), `\"tdd\"` — used for grouping and filtering diagram entries\n6. `_plan.json` includes `\"architecture\": { \"ref\": \"./arch/_arch.json\" }` at the top level\n7. Plan JSON no longer requires `uiFlows`, `dataModels`, `dataFlow`, `services` sections - these are replaced by arch/ files\n\n### Non-Functional\n\n- **Performance:** Manifest file < 10KB (metadata only, no content)\n- **Platform:** File system (cross-platform paths)\n\n## User Workflows\n\n### Workflow 1: Agent Generates Architecture\n\n**Actor:** AI agent (via /vista:plan)\n**Trigger:** Step 5 of plan workflow\n\n**Steps:**\n1. Agent creates `arch/` directory\n2. Agent writes .mmd files for each diagram (system-arch, user-flow, sequence, state-model, data-model)\n3. Agent writes `_arch.json` manifest referencing each file\n4. Agent writes `_plan.json` with `architecture.ref` pointing to manifest\n5. Feature directory is complete\n\n**Error Cases:**\n- Invalid Mermaid syntax in .mmd file: Web renderer shows parse error inline\n- Missing file referenced in manifest: Web app shows \"File not found\" placeholder\n\n### Workflow 2: User Adds Diagram Manually\n\n**Actor:** Developer\n**Trigger:** User wants to add a diagram outside the plan workflow\n\n**Steps:**\n1. User creates a .mmd or .drawio file in arch/\n2. User adds an entry to _arch.json manually or via CLI\n3. Web app picks up the new diagram on next page load\n\n**Error Cases:**\n- Malformed _arch.json: Server returns 400 with validation error\n\n## Data Model\n\n**Entities:**\n- ArchManifest: `{ feature: string, diagrams: DiagramEntry[] }`\n- DiagramEntry: `{ name: string, file: string, type: \"mermaid\"|\"drawio\", diagramType: string, category?: \"architecture\"|\"tdd\", description: string }`\n\n**Relationships:**\n- ArchManifest 1:N DiagramEntry\n- Feature 1:1 ArchManifest (via _plan.json reference)\n\n## Integration Points\n\n**Dependencies:**\n- setup-feature.py: Must scaffold arch/ directory and empty _arch.json\n\n**Provides to:**\n- Rendering pipeline: Manifest tells the web app what to render and how\n- Chat review: Manifest provides diagram list for context injection\n\n## Technical Considerations\n\n### Architecture\n- File system layer only - no database\n- JSON schema validation for _arch.json\n\n### Patterns\n- Manifest pattern (registry of files, not container of content)\n- Reference pattern (_plan.json -> _arch.json)\n\n### Libraries/APIs\n- Python `json` for manifest read/write\n- `pathlib` for cross-platform path handling\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [x] `setup-feature.py --name X` creates `arch/` directory and empty `_arch.json`\n- [x] `_arch.json` validates against defined schema\n- [x] `_plan.json` includes `architecture.ref` field\n- [x] Plan JSON schema no longer requires uiFlows, dataModels, dataFlow, services sections\n- [x] Server API can read _arch.json and return manifest data\n- [x] Server API can read individual diagram file contents by manifest entry\n\n## Implementation Notes\n\n- `arch-schema.json` has been extended beyond this spec's original definition. The `diagramType` enum now includes TDD-related types (`logic-flow`, `decision-tree`, `test-contract`) and a `category` field (`architecture` | `tdd`) for grouping.\n- Path traversal protection is implemented in `ProgressService.read_arch_file()` using both filename sanitization and resolved path validation.\n\n## Resolved Questions\n\n- _arch.json supports grouping via a `category` field on each diagram entry (values: `architecture`, `tdd`).\n","numLines":124,"startLine":1,"totalLines":124}}}
