{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01N925tz4Rg17T7NMCptCm1V","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# Implementation Plan: Multi-Format Diagram Support & Markdown Editing (Build)\n     2→\n     3→**Source Plan:** `.vista/ralph/diagram-repr-spec-planning/IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md`\n     4→**Status:** IN PROGRESS — Iteration 2 complete (Phases 1-4 done, Phase 5 partial, Phase 6 remaining)\n     5→\n     6→---\n     7→\n     8→## Phase 1: Schema & Backend Foundation — DONE (Iteration 1)\n     9→\n    10→- [x] 1.1 Extend arch-schema.json type enum (6 values)\n    11→- [x] 1.2 Add write_arch_file() to ProgressService (.md-only whitelist)\n    12→- [x] 1.3 Add PUT endpoint for file writing\n    13→- [x] 1.4 Update content-type mapping in GET endpoint (dictionary-based)\n    14→- [x] 1.5 Add PlantUML server URL to settings (config.py)\n    15→- [x] 1.6 Extend diagram watcher extensions (both WATCH_EXTENSIONS, EXT_TO_TYPE, _detect_file_type, _update_manifest_sync)\n    16→\n    17→**Deviation:** Non-mermaid files now get `diagramType: \"custom\"` instead of their format name (e.g., drawio files were previously \"drawio\", now \"custom\"). This is more consistent — diagramType is for Mermaid subtypes.\n    18→\n    19→## Phase 5 (partial): Backend Tests — DONE (Iteration 1)\n    20→\n    21→- [x] 5.1 PUT endpoint tests (7 tests in TestArchWriteAPI)\n    22→- [x] 5.2 ProgressService write tests (6 tests in TestProgressServiceWrite)\n    23→- [x] 5.3 Extended schema validation tests (4 tests in TestExtendedSchemaValidation)\n    24→- [x] 5.4 Content-type tests (4 tests in TestContentTypes)\n    25→- [x] 5.5 Diagram watcher extension tests (16 tests in TestExtendedFileTypes)\n    26→- [x] 5.6 Settings tests (2 tests in TestDiagramSettings)\n    27→- [x] Updated existing test_drawio_type to expect \"custom\" diagramType\n    28→\n    29→**Total tests:** 95 passing (53 arch + 42 watcher)\n    30→\n    31→---\n    32→\n    33→## Phase 2: Client-Side Renderer Infrastructure — DONE (Iteration 2)\n    34→\n    35→- [x] 2.1 Refactor renderer dispatch in architecture.html (RENDERERS map with type-based dispatch)\n    36→- [x] 2.2 Extract Mermaid renderer into standalone renderMermaid() function\n    37→- [x] 2.3 PlantUML renderer (plantuml-encoder CDN + PLANTUML_SERVER_URL server fetch)\n    38→- [x] 2.4 D2 renderer (raw source display + optional Kroki server integration)\n    39→- [x] 2.5 Graphviz renderer (lazy-loaded @viz-js/viz@3.11.0 WASM)\n    40→- [x] 2.6 Draw.io renderer (iframe via viewer.diagrams.net with base64 encoding)\n    41→- [x] 2.7 Markdown renderer (marked.js with rawContent dataset storage for edit mode)\n    42→\n    43→**Learnings:**\n    44→- Extension-based type inference added as fallback when `diagramType` is not provided (for backwards compatibility)\n    45→- Draw.io uses base64-encoded URL; large files may need postMessage API in future\n    46→- Graphviz WASM loads lazily via dynamic script injection on first .dot diagram render\n    47→\n    48→## Phase 3: Markdown Inline Editor — DONE (Iteration 2)\n    49→\n    50→- [x] 3.1 Edit button on markdown cards (Jinja2 template + JS dynamic cards)\n    51→- [x] 3.2 Edit mode state machine (view → editing → saving → view) with markdownEditState tracking\n    52→- [x] 3.3 Keyboard shortcuts (Ctrl+S/Cmd+S save, Escape cancel)\n    53→- [x] 3.4 Editor CSS styles (md-editor-container, toolbar, textarea, save/cancel buttons, indicators)\n    54→\n    55→**Implementation notes:**\n    56→- DIAGRAMS array is 0-indexed but element IDs use 1-indexed (idx = loop.index in Jinja2)\n    57→- Save indicator shows \"Saving...\" → \"Saved!\" → auto-switch to rendered view after 800ms\n    58→- autoResizeTextarea() dynamically adjusts height with 200px minimum\n    59→\n    60→## Phase 4: Template & Watcher Integration — DONE (Iteration 2)\n    61→\n    62→- [x] 4.1 Pass manifest type to renderers in loadDiagrams() (5th argument)\n    63→- [x] 4.2 Conditionally show edit button in card header (Jinja2 + addDiagramCard JS)\n    64→- [x] 4.3 CDN script loading (plantuml-encoder@1.4.0 eager, viz-js lazy)\n    65→- [x] 4.4 PlantUML server URL injection (done in architecture.py route, Iteration 1)\n    66→\n    67→**Additional changes:**\n    68→- updateDiagram() and addDiagramCard() now pass diagram.type to renderDiagramContent()\n    69→- addDiagramCard() infers type from file extension for dynamically added diagrams\n    70→- PLANTUML_SERVER_URL JS constant injected via Jinja2 `{{ plantuml_url | tojson }}`\n    71→- Rendered markdown content CSS styles added to arch-chat.css\n    72→\n    73→---\n    74→\n    75→## Phase 5 (remainder): Integration Tests — TODO (Iteration 3)\n    76→\n    77→- [ ] Integration tests for full render pipeline (requires browser-based testing)\n    78→\n    79→## Phase 6: Documentation & Skill Updates — TODO (Iteration 3)\n    80→\n    81→- [ ] 6.1 Update plan skill SKILL.md\n    82→- [ ] 6.2 Update diagrams skill\n    83→- [ ] 6.3 Update specs (arch-directory.md, rendering-pipeline.md)\n    84→"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d91d5e1b-c8a8-412a-adba-876f560ccc8f","uuid":"208ec467-62c6-4520-b394-49dce564b2ed","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:/Users/Grove/OneDrive/Documents/PYTHON/claude_plugins/vista-expanded-visualization/.vista/ralph/diagram-repr-spec-build/IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md","content":"# Implementation Plan: Multi-Format Diagram Support & Markdown Editing (Build)\n\n**Source Plan:** `.vista/ralph/diagram-repr-spec-planning/IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md`\n**Status:** IN PROGRESS — Iteration 2 complete (Phases 1-4 done, Phase 5 partial, Phase 6 remaining)\n\n---\n\n## Phase 1: Schema & Backend Foundation — DONE (Iteration 1)\n\n- [x] 1.1 Extend arch-schema.json type enum (6 values)\n- [x] 1.2 Add write_arch_file() to ProgressService (.md-only whitelist)\n- [x] 1.3 Add PUT endpoint for file writing\n- [x] 1.4 Update content-type mapping in GET endpoint (dictionary-based)\n- [x] 1.5 Add PlantUML server URL to settings (config.py)\n- [x] 1.6 Extend diagram watcher extensions (both WATCH_EXTENSIONS, EXT_TO_TYPE, _detect_file_type, _update_manifest_sync)\n\n**Deviation:** Non-mermaid files now get `diagramType: \"custom\"` instead of their format name (e.g., drawio files were previously \"drawio\", now \"custom\"). This is more consistent — diagramType is for Mermaid subtypes.\n\n## Phase 5 (partial): Backend Tests — DONE (Iteration 1)\n\n- [x] 5.1 PUT endpoint tests (7 tests in TestArchWriteAPI)\n- [x] 5.2 ProgressService write tests (6 tests in TestProgressServiceWrite)\n- [x] 5.3 Extended schema validation tests (4 tests in TestExtendedSchemaValidation)\n- [x] 5.4 Content-type tests (4 tests in TestContentTypes)\n- [x] 5.5 Diagram watcher extension tests (16 tests in TestExtendedFileTypes)\n- [x] 5.6 Settings tests (2 tests in TestDiagramSettings)\n- [x] Updated existing test_drawio_type to expect \"custom\" diagramType\n\n**Total tests:** 95 passing (53 arch + 42 watcher)\n\n---\n\n## Phase 2: Client-Side Renderer Infrastructure — DONE (Iteration 2)\n\n- [x] 2.1 Refactor renderer dispatch in architecture.html (RENDERERS map with type-based dispatch)\n- [x] 2.2 Extract Mermaid renderer into standalone renderMermaid() function\n- [x] 2.3 PlantUML renderer (plantuml-encoder CDN + PLANTUML_SERVER_URL server fetch)\n- [x] 2.4 D2 renderer (raw source display + optional Kroki server integration)\n- [x] 2.5 Graphviz renderer (lazy-loaded @viz-js/viz@3.11.0 WASM)\n- [x] 2.6 Draw.io renderer (iframe via viewer.diagrams.net with base64 encoding)\n- [x] 2.7 Markdown renderer (marked.js with rawContent dataset storage for edit mode)\n\n**Learnings:**\n- Extension-based type inference added as fallback when `diagramType` is not provided (for backwards compatibility)\n- Draw.io uses base64-encoded URL; large files may need postMessage API in future\n- Graphviz WASM loads lazily via dynamic script injection on first .dot diagram render\n\n## Phase 3: Markdown Inline Editor — DONE (Iteration 2)\n\n- [x] 3.1 Edit button on markdown cards (Jinja2 template + JS dynamic cards)\n- [x] 3.2 Edit mode state machine (view → editing → saving → view) with markdownEditState tracking\n- [x] 3.3 Keyboard shortcuts (Ctrl+S/Cmd+S save, Escape cancel)\n- [x] 3.4 Editor CSS styles (md-editor-container, toolbar, textarea, save/cancel buttons, indicators)\n\n**Implementation notes:**\n- DIAGRAMS array is 0-indexed but element IDs use 1-indexed (idx = loop.index in Jinja2)\n- Save indicator shows \"Saving...\" → \"Saved!\" → auto-switch to rendered view after 800ms\n- autoResizeTextarea() dynamically adjusts height with 200px minimum\n\n## Phase 4: Template & Watcher Integration — DONE (Iteration 2)\n\n- [x] 4.1 Pass manifest type to renderers in loadDiagrams() (5th argument)\n- [x] 4.2 Conditionally show edit button in card header (Jinja2 + addDiagramCard JS)\n- [x] 4.3 CDN script loading (plantuml-encoder@1.4.0 eager, viz-js lazy)\n- [x] 4.4 PlantUML server URL injection (done in architecture.py route, Iteration 1)\n\n**Additional changes:**\n- updateDiagram() and addDiagramCard() now pass diagram.type to renderDiagramContent()\n- addDiagramCard() infers type from file extension for dynamically added diagrams\n- PLANTUML_SERVER_URL JS constant injected via Jinja2 `{{ plantuml_url | tojson }}`\n- Rendered markdown content CSS styles added to arch-chat.css\n\n---\n\n## Phase 5 (remainder): Integration Tests — TODO (Iteration 3)\n\n- [ ] Integration tests for full render pipeline (requires browser-based testing)\n\n## Phase 6: Documentation & Skill Updates — TODO (Iteration 3)\n\n- [ ] 6.1 Update plan skill SKILL.md\n- [ ] 6.2 Update diagrams skill\n- [ ] 6.3 Update specs (arch-directory.md, rendering-pipeline.md)\n","numLines":84,"startLine":1,"totalLines":84}}}
